{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793742356729,"sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","part":{"partID":"prt_1a36040cb0013j5eAH5K6TP2sn","sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","messageID":"msg_1a3600ede001tHagU17048prKT","type":"tool","id":"call_01_4ykwosi2wx6655vi1hwqvu9a","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '1,80p' .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md"},"output":"---\ntitle: Skill Reference File Templates\ndescription: Comprehensive templates for creating effective reference files for AI agent skills with workflows, decision logic, and validation checkpoints.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"skill reference templates\"\n  - \"reference file structure\"\n  - \"explicit reasoning references\"\n  - \"reference creation guidelines\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: general\nversion: 1.2.0.25\n---\n\n# Skill Reference File Templates - AI Agent Skills\n\nTemplates for creating reference files in AI agent skills with deep-dive technical guidance.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Location & Naming\n\n**Location:** `.skilled/skills/[skill-name]/references/`\n\n**Naming Convention:** kebab-case with `.md` extension only\n\n| ✅ Valid Names | ❌ Invalid Names |\n|---------------|-----------------|\n| `implementation-workflows.md` | `ImplementationWorkflows.md` (PascalCase) |\n| `tool-catalog.md` | `tool_catalog.md` (snake_case) |\n| `debugging-guide.md` | `DebuggingGuide.MD` (wrong case) |\n| `quick-reference.md` | `quickReference.md` (camelCase) |\n| `code-quality-standards.md` | `code quality standards.md` (spaces) |\n\n### When to Create References\n\n**Create a reference file when:**\n- Multi-phase workflows with validation checkpoints\n- Decision trees with multiple branches\n- Pattern libraries with 5+ variations\n- Systematic debugging procedures\n- Tool integration details\n- Content exceeds 200 lines\n\n**Keep in SKILL.md when:**\n- Content under 200 lines\n- Simple workflows (3-5 steps)\n- Overview and \"When to Use\" sections\n- Essential rules (ALWAYS/NEVER/ESCALATE IF)\n\n---\n\n## 2. DOCUMENT STRUCTURE\n\n### Document Structure: Title and Intro\n\n**CRITICAL: The intro after the H1 title must be 1-2 SHORT sentences only.**\n\n```markdown\n---\ntitle: [Title]\ndescription: [One-line description - same as intro]\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"[distinctive phrase one]\"\n  - \"[distinctive phrase two]\"\n  - \"[distinctive phrase three]\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: general\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n---\n\n# [Title]\n\n[1-2 SHORT sentences only. Brief hook/summary. NO subsections, NO headers here.]\n\n---\n\n\\## 1. OVERVIEW\n[All detailed content goes here, NOT in the intro]\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: Skill Reference File Templates\ndescription: Comprehensive templates for creating effective reference files for AI agent skills with workflows, decision logic, and validation checkpoints.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"skill reference templates\"\n  - \"reference file structure\"\n  - \"explicit reasoning references\"\n  - \"reference creation guidelines\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: general\nversion: 1.2.0.25\n---\n\n# Skill Reference File Templates - AI Agent Skills\n\nTemplates for creating reference files in AI agent skills with deep-dive technical guidance.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Location & Naming\n\n**Location:** `.skilled/skills/[skill-name]/references/`\n\n**Naming Convention:** kebab-case with `.md` extension only\n\n| ✅ Valid Names | ❌ Invalid Names |\n|---------------|-----------------|\n| `implementation-workflows.md` | `ImplementationWorkflows.md` (PascalCase) |\n| `tool-catalog.md` | `tool_catalog.md` (snake_case) |\n| `debugging-guide.md` | `DebuggingGuide.MD` (wrong case) |\n| `quick-reference.md` | `quickReference.md` (camelCase) |\n| `code-quality-standards.md` | `code quality standards.md` (spaces) |\n\n### When to Create References\n\n**Create a reference file when:**\n- Multi-phase workflows with validation checkpoints\n- Decision trees with multiple branches\n- Pattern libraries with 5+ variations\n- Systematic debugging procedures\n- Tool integration details\n- Content exceeds 200 lines\n\n**Keep in SKILL.md when:**\n- Content under 200 lines\n- Simple workflows (3-5 steps)\n- Overview and \"When to Use\" sections\n- Essential rules (ALWAYS/NEVER/ESCALATE IF)\n\n---\n\n## 2. DOCUMENT STRUCTURE\n\n### Document Structure: Title and Intro\n\n**CRITICAL: The intro after the H1 title must be 1-2 SHORT sentences only.**\n\n```markdown\n---\ntitle: [Title]\ndescription: [One-line description - same as intro]\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"[distinctive phrase one]\"\n  - \"[distinctive phrase two]\"\n  - \"[distinctive phrase three]\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: general\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n---\n\n# [Title]\n\n[1-2 SHORT sentences only. Brief hook/summary. NO subsections, NO headers here.]\n\n---\n\n\\## 1. OVERVIEW\n[All detailed content goes here, NOT in the intro]\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"sed -n '1,80p' .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793742356683,"end":1793742356729}}}}
