{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793742383773,"sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","part":{"partID":"prt_1a360a966001Aq4pyUdaFJneUg","sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","messageID":"msg_1a3608197001Pcc0yibjKZK6x8","type":"tool","id":"call_00_aqqwyuedreh3gazadegr838i","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - sk-code Reference Readability Audit\ndescription: Tracks the eight-iteration audit of reference/asset readability, section order and rendering defects across the sk-code skill family, plus the sk-doc template and validator gap analysis.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"sk-code reference readability\"\n  - \"markdown rendering defect audit\"\n  - \"sk-doc template gap\"\n  - \"validator coverage gaps\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: research\nversion: 1.0.0.0\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent brain for the detached deepseek lineage: records the audit focus, what evidence worked, what failed, and where the next iteration should look.\n\n### Usage\n\n- **Init:** Focus questions and boundaries seeded from the dispatch topic.\n- **Per iteration:** the iteration file carries the evidence; the reducer refreshes the machine-owned sections below.\n- **Mutability:** analyst-owned sections are stable; machine-owned sections are projections.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\nAudit every reference and asset under `.skilled/skills/sk-code/` for readability, structure, layout and section/item order against the sk-doc reference and asset templates; find rendering defects; trace why the sk-doc templates, authoring guidance and `validate_document.py` let them pass; propose mechanically checkable fixes.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\nGenerated from the reducer registry.\n\n- [ ] What section-order and container contract does the sk-doc skill-reference template define, and how do the six sk-code SKILL.md and ROUTER.md files plus hub shared references diverge from it?\n- [ ] Which sk-code-ci references and assets violate heading shape, section order or item order, and at which exact lines?\n- [ ] Which sk-code-frontend references, including web-cascade-and-selectors.md, carry the enumerated rendering defects, and at which exact lines?\n- [ ] Which sk-code-quality references carry the enumerated rendering defects or structural divergence, and at which exact lines?\n- [ ] Which sk-code-review references and assets carry the enumerated rendering defects or structural divergence, and at which exact lines?\n- [ ] Which sk-code-skilled references and checklist assets carry the enumerated defects, and is the divergence systematic across a file family?\n- [ ] Why do the sk-doc templates, authoring guidance and validate_document.py fail to detect each defect class, traced check by check?\n- [ ] Which template, guidance and validator changes would catch each defect class, and which are mechanically checkable at what precision?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n- Editing any sk-code or sk-doc file: this lineage is read-only outside its artifact directory.\n- Reviewing manual-testing-playbook, changelog, benchmark or feature-catalog prose except where a reference/asset under audit links to it.\n- Judging whether the technical guidance is correct; only readability, structure, layout, order and the validator gap.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n- Eight iterations completed (`stopPolicy: max-iterations`), regardless of convergence telemetry.\n- Confirm every defect class has at least one confirmed file:line instance and one validator-gap explanation.\n- Missing evidence for a claim forces an explicit UNKNOWN, never a silent generalization.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n[Populated after iteration 1]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n[Populated after iteration 1]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[None yet]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[None yet]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[None yet]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nIteration 1: establish the template contract, then audit the hub root files (SKILL.md, ROUTER.md, shared/references).\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n- Audit corpus: 6 SKILL.md, 6 ROUTER.md, ~70 reference files, ~25 asset/checklist files under `.skilled/skills/sk-code/`.\n- Baseline templates: `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md` and `skill-asset-template.md`.\n- Validator: `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py`.\n- A mechanical structural scanner is staged under the lineage `.executor-state/` directory to find candidate defects with line numbers; every candidate still needs a manual read before it becomes a finding.\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n- Source pointers: `sk-code/references/*`, `sk-code/*/references/*`, `sk-code/*/assets/*`, `sk-code/SKILL.md`, `sk-code/*/SKILL.md`, `sk-code/ROUTER.md`, `sk-code/*/ROUTER.md`.\n- Reuse candidates: sk-doc templates as the normative baseline; `validate_document.py` as the coverage subject.\n- Integration points: template guidance, `sk-create-skill` scripts, validator checks.\n- Constraints: read-only outside the lineage; every finding needs a file:line citation.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n- Max iterations: 8\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05 (telemetry only; stopPolicy is max-iterations)\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 20 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: false\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause` inside the lineage artifact directory\n- Started: 2026-11-03T21:45:56Z\n","path":"specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"---\\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - sk-code Reference Readability Audit\\ndescription: Tracks the eight-iteration audit of reference/asset readability, section order and rendering defects across the sk-code skill family, plus the sk-doc template and validator gap analysis.\\ntrigger_phrases:\\n  - \\\"sk-code reference readability\\\"\\n  - \\\"markdown rendering defect audit\\\"\\n  - \\\"sk-doc template gap\\\"\\n  - \\\"validator coverage gaps\\\"\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: research\\nversion: 1.0.0.0\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent brain for the detached deepseek lineage: records the audit focus, what evidence worked, what failed, and where the next iteration should look.\\n\\n### Usage\\n\\n- **Init:** Focus questions and boundaries seeded from the dispatch topic.\\n- **Per iteration:** the iteration file carries the evidence; the reducer refreshes the machine-owned sections below.\\n- **Mutability:** analyst-owned sections are stable; machine-owned sections are projections.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\nAudit every reference and asset under `.skilled/skills/sk-code/` for readability, structure, layout and section/item order against the sk-doc reference and asset templates; find rendering defects; trace why the sk-doc templates, authoring guidance and `validate_document.py` let them pass; propose mechanically checkable fixes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\nGenerated from the reducer registry.\\n\\n- [ ] What section-order and container contract does the sk-doc skill-reference template define, and how do the six sk-code SKILL.md and ROUTER.md files plus hub shared references diverge from it?\\n- [ ] Which sk-code-ci references and assets violate heading shape, section order or item order, and at which exact lines?\\n- [ ] Which sk-code-frontend references, including web-cascade-and-selectors.md, carry the enumerated rendering defects, and at which exact lines?\\n- [ ] Which sk-code-quality references carry the enumerated rendering defects or structural divergence, and at which exact lines?\\n- [ ] Which sk-code-review references and assets carry the enumerated rendering defects or structural divergence, and at which exact lines?\\n- [ ] Which sk-code-skilled references and checklist assets carry the enumerated defects, and is the divergence systematic across a file family?\\n- [ ] Why do the sk-doc templates, authoring guidance and validate_document.py fail to detect each defect class, traced check by check?\\n- [ ] Which template, guidance and validator changes would catch each defect class, and which are mechanically checkable at what precision?\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n- Editing any sk-code or sk-doc file: this lineage is read-only outside its artifact directory.\\n- Reviewing manual-testing-playbook, changelog, benchmark or feature-catalog prose except where a reference/asset under audit links to it.\\n- Judging whether the technical guidance is correct; only readability, structure, layout, order and the validator gap.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n- Eight iterations completed (`stopPolicy: max-iterations`), regardless of convergence telemetry.\\n- Confirm every defect class has at least one confirmed file:line instance and one validator-gap explanation.\\n- Missing evidence for a claim forces an explicit UNKNOWN, never a silent generalization.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n[None yet]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n[Populated after iteration 1]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n[Populated after iteration 1]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n[None yet]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n[None yet]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\\n[None yet]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\nIteration 1: establish the template contract, then audit the hub root files (SKILL.md, ROUTER.md, shared/references).\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n- Audit corpus: 6 SKILL.md, 6 ROUTER.md, ~70 reference files, ~25 asset/checklist files under `.skilled/skills/sk-code/`.\\n- Baseline templates: `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md` and `skill-asset-template.md`.\\n- Validator: `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py`.\\n- A mechanical structural scanner is staged under the lineage `.executor-state/` directory to find candidate defects with line numbers; every candidate still needs a manual read before it becomes a finding.\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n- Source pointers: `sk-code/references/*`, `sk-code/*/references/*`, `sk-code/*/assets/*`, `sk-code/SKILL.md`, `sk-code/*/SKILL.md`, `sk-code/ROUTER.md`, `sk-code/*/ROUTER.md`.\\n- Reuse candidates: sk-doc templates as the normative baseline; `validate_document.py` as the coverage subject.\\n- Integration points: template guidance, `sk-create-skill` scripts, validator checks.\\n- Constraints: read-only outside the lineage; every finding needs a file:line citation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\\n- Max iterations: 8\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05 (telemetry only; stopPolicy is max-iterations)\\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 20 minutes\\n- Progressive synthesis: false\\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause` inside the lineage artifact directory\\n- Started: 2026-11-03T21:45:56Z\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793742383462,"