{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793742647280,"sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","part":{"id":"prt_1a364aff0001qF6050LYtUQIaB","sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","messageID":"msg_1a364a9ec0019dMG5E6c0JUApB","type":"step-start","snapshot":"f51c493a61e015dd34511c34cd94b1ede1a58f61"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793742652024,"sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","part":{"partID":"prt_1a364c21b001PnQKAzibguczR3","sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","messageID":"msg_1a364a9ec0019dMG5E6c0JUApB","type":"tool","id":"call_01_dlv7sf3syd6xku53tprmfezj","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"=== PRE-FIX BOLD LABELS ===\"; grep -n '^\\*\\*' specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/.executor-state/prefix-web-cascade.md | head -20; echo \"=== PRE-FIX BARE URLS ===\"; grep -n '^\\*\\*See also\\.\\*\\* https' specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/.executor-state/prefix-web-cascade.md | head; echo \"=== CURRENT ADJACENT BOLD ===\"; grep -n -B1 '^\\*\\*' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/*.md | head -20"},"output":"=== PRE-FIX BOLD LABELS ===\n23:**Rule.** Resolve competing declarations by origin and importance, layer order, specificity, scope proximity when scoped rules apply, then source order.\n24:**Why.** The cascade compares these criteria in order, so a later rule cannot win by source order when an earlier criterion already decided the result.\n25:**When not to.** Skip the comparison when the declarations do not apply to the same element and property.\n26:**Pitfall.** Normal unlayered declarations outrank normal declarations in named layers, while important declarations reverse layer precedence.\n27:**Support.** Judgment, no version gate.\n28:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Cascade\n32:**Rule.** Declare the cascade layer order once in a global stylesheet before component styles load.\n33:**Why.** Layer order is established the first time each layer name appears. Component style injection can vary with load order, so per-component layer blocks cannot define a reliable shared order.\n34:**When not to.** Use unlayered styles only when the app deliberately relies on the unlayered precedence boundary.\n35:**Pitfall.** A deeply scoped rule inside a layer loses to an unlayered rule even when its selector looks stronger.\n36:**Support.** Baseline widely available since 2024-09-14 (web-features `cascade-layers`). Chrome 99 / Firefox 97 / Safari 15.4.\n37:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@layer\n41:**Rule.** Count IDs, class-like selectors and type selectors in separate specificity columns before changing a selector.\n42:**Why.** IDs add to the first column, classes, attributes and pseudo-classes add to the second, and type selectors and pseudo-elements add to the third. A component-scoping attribute such as `[data-scope]` adds one class-like unit.\n43:**When not to.** Do not raise specificity when the actual conflict comes from origin, importance or cascade layer order.\n44:**Pitfall.** A selector such as `.card[data-scope]` has specificity `0-2-0`, not `0-1-0`.\n45:**Support.** Judgment, no version gate.\n46:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Specificity\n54:**Rule.** Wrap low-priority defaults in `:where()` and use `:is()` when the matching alternatives should share the strongest argument's specificity.\n55:**Why.** `:where()` contributes zero specificity, while `:is()` contributes the specificity of its most specific argument.\n=== PRE-FIX BARE URLS ===\n28:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Cascade\n37:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@layer\n46:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Specificity\n60:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/:is\n69:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/:has\n82:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_nesting/Using_CSS_nesting\n91:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@scope\n100:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@property\n109:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Attribute_selectors\n=== CURRENT ADJACENT BOLD ===\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/frontend-practice.md-94-\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/frontend-practice.md:95:**Layers**\n--\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/frontend-practice.md-101-\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/frontend-practice.md:102:**Web topic files**\n--\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md-57-\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md:58:**Deeper:** [Elements and attributes](web-elements-and-attributes.md) and [accessibility patterns](web-accessibility-patterns.md).\n--\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md-72-\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md:73:**The `autocomplete` disagreement.** `interaction-craft.md` Section 2 advises disabling `autocomplete` on most inputs. That holds for free-text fields where browser history adds noise, such as comments, in-app search filters and admin entry of someone else's data. It does not hold for fields about the user. Identity, contact, address, payment and credential fields need the right token so autofill and password managers work and the input purpose is machine-readable:\n--\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md-84-\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md:85:**Deeper:** [Elements and attributes](web-elements-and-attributes.md).\n--\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md-100-\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md:101:**Deeper:** [Layout and sizing](web-layout-and-sizing.md) and [internationalization](web-internationalization.md).\n--\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md-116-\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md:117:**Deeper:** [Layout and sizing](web-layout-and-sizing.md) and [accessibility patterns](web-accessibility-patterns.md).\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== PRE-FIX BOLD LABELS ===\n23:**Rule.** Resolve competing declarations by origin and importance, layer order, specificity, scope proximity when scoped rules apply, then source order.\n24:**Why.** The cascade compares these criteria in order, so a later rule cannot win by source order when an earlier criterion already decided the result.\n25:**When not to.** Skip the comparison when the declarations do not apply to the same element and property.\n26:**Pitfall.** Normal unlayered declarations outrank normal declarations in named layers, while important declarations reverse layer precedence.\n27:**Support.** Judgment, no version gate.\n28:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Cascade\n32:**Rule.** Declare the cascade layer order once in a global stylesheet before component styles load.\n33:**Why.** Layer order is established the first time each layer name appears. Component style injection can vary with load order, so per-component layer blocks cannot define a reliable shared order.\n34:**When not to.** Use unlayered styles only when the app deliberately relies on the unlayered precedence boundary.\n35:**Pitfall.** A deeply scoped rule inside a layer loses to an unlayered rule even when its selector looks stronger.\n36:**Support.** Baseline widely available since 2024-09-14 (web-features `cascade-layers`). Chrome 99 / Firefox 97 / Safari 15.4.\n37:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@layer\n41:**Rule.** Count IDs, class-like selectors and type selectors in separate specificity columns before changing a selector.\n42:**Why.** IDs add to the first column, classes, attributes and pseudo-classes add to the second, and type selectors and pseudo-elements add to the third. A component-scoping attribute such as `[data-scope]` adds one class-like unit.\n43:**When not to.** Do not raise specificity when the actual conflict comes from origin, importance or cascade layer order.\n44:**Pitfall.** A selector such as `.card[data-scope]` has specificity `0-2-0`, not `0-1-0`.\n45:**Support.** Judgment, no version gate.\n46:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Specificity\n54:**Rule.** Wrap low-priority defaults in `:where()` and use `:is()` when the matching alternatives should share the strongest argument's specificity.\n55:**Why.** `:where()` contributes zero specificity, while `:is()` contributes the specificity of its most specific argument.\n=== PRE-FIX BARE URLS ===\n28:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Cascade\n37:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@layer\n46:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Specificity\n60:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/:is\n69:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/:has\n82:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_nesting/Using_CSS_nesting\n91:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@scope\n100:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@property\n109:**See also.** https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Attribute_selectors\n=== CURRENT ADJACENT BOLD ===\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/frontend-practice.md-94-\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/frontend-practice.md:95:**Layers**\n--\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/frontend-practice.md-101-\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/frontend-practice.md:102:**Web topic files**\n--\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md-57-\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md:58:**Deeper:** [Elements and attributes](web-elements-and-attributes.md) and [accessibility patterns](web-accessibility-patterns.md).\n--\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md-72-\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md:73:**The `autocomplete` disagreement.** `interaction-craft.md` Section 2 advises disabling `autocomplete` on most inputs. That holds for free-text fields where browser history adds noise, such as comments, in-app search filters and admin entry of someone else's data. It does not hold for fields about the user. Identity, contact, address, payment and credential fields need the right token so autofill and password managers work and the input purpose is machine-readable:\n--\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md-84-\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md:85:**Deeper:** [Elements and attributes](web-elements-and-attributes.md).\n--\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md-100-\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md:101:**Deeper:** [Layout and sizing](web-layout-and-sizing.md) and [internationalization](web-internationalization.md).\n--\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md-116-\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-markup-and-css.md:117:**Deeper:** [Layout and sizing](web-layout-and-sizing.md) and [accessibility patterns](web-accessibility-patterns.md).\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"echo \\\"=== PRE-FIX BOLD LABELS ===\\\"; grep -n '^\\\\*\\\\*' specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/.executor-state/prefix-web-cascade.md | head -20; echo \\\"=== PRE-FIX BARE URLS ===\\\"; grep -n '^\\\\*\\\\*See