{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793742659391,"sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","part":{"partID":"prt_1a364de8e001exf4EM1chATaMx","sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","messageID":"msg_1a364c534001fETT8XpkhEZIKA","type":"tool","id":"call_00_zfmhedmoj3c5hw1njvnvo2fd","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '10,28p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md; echo \"===FIGMA 13-40===\"; sed -n '13,40p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/figma-to-code.md; echo \"===I18N 105-125===\"; sed -n '105,125p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-internationalization.md; echo \"===PERF 105-135===\"; sed -n '105,135p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md"},"output":"router_state: active\nskill_pointer: SKILL.md\n---\n\n# Frontend Surface Router\n\nThe machine router for [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md). The core reference is the default resource; each intent adds the web layer or Figma check it needs.\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThis surface holds the core in `references/frontend-practice.md`, the web layer in `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, six web topic files, and the five-pass Figma check in `references/figma-to-code.md`. Every intent loads the core and the matching web or Figma-to-code layer. Topic files load when the request touches their listed concern.\n\n### Web Topic Files\n\n| Topic | File | Load when |\n|---|---|---|\n| Elements and attributes | [web-elements-and-attributes.md](references/web-elements-and-attributes.md) | Adding or changing a dialog, popover, disclosure, form-control attribute, or resource hint |\n| Cascade and selectors | [web-cascade-and-selectors.md](references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md) | Changing selector reach, cascade layers, specificity, or component style boundaries |\n| Layout and sizing | [web-layout-and-sizing.md](references/web-layout-and-sizing.md) | Changing stacking, containing blocks, intrinsic sizing, container queries, or scrolling |\n===FIGMA 13-40===\n# Figma to Code Translation\n\nHow to read a Figma design as a reference and build the simplest correct structure from it.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Core Principle\n\nFigma is a reference for code, never its markup. Never copy the layer tree, absolute coordinates, fixed frame sizes or component property sets 1:1 into code.\n\n### Purpose\n\nA Figma read, export or MCP pull tells you what the screen should look like and which states it has. It does not tell you which elements to write.\n\n### When to Use\n\n- Reading a Figma frame before writing code\n- Translating auto layout, sizing or absolute layers into CSS\n- Mapping Figma variables and styles to installed tokens\n- Running the five-pass check against a rendered build\n- Reporting a Figma-to-code red flag\n\n### Boundaries\n\nThis file does not own:\n\n===I18N 105-125===\n### I7. Date-only parsing\n\n- **Rule:** Parse date-only values as calendar dates in the intended locale and time zone instead of converting them through UTC timestamps.\n- **Why:** JavaScript parses an ISO date-only string such as `2026-11-02` at UTC midnight, which can display as the previous local date in a negative offset.\n- **When not to:** Use a timestamp when the input represents an exact instant rather than a calendar date.\n- **Pitfall:** Calling `toISOString().slice(0, 10)` on a local date can serialize a different calendar day.\n- **Support:** Judgment, no version gate.\n- **See also:** [MDN: Date.parse()](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Date/parse)\n\n---\n\n## 5. TRANSLATION-TOLERANT TEXT\n\n### I9. Expansion and pseudo-localization\n\n- **Rule:** Test layouts with pseudo-localized text and leave room for German and Dutch strings that can grow by about 30 to 35 percent.\n- **Why:** Translation changes word length and line breaks, which can push fixed-width controls past their available space.\n- **When not to:** Use a fixed measure only when the content has a documented hard limit, such as a machine identifier.\n- **Pitfall:** A button that fits the source language can clip its translated label when its width is fixed.\n- **Support:** Judgment, no version gate.\n- **See also:** [MDN: Localization and plurals](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Localization/Localization_and_Plurals)\n===PERF 105-135===\n- **Why:** The hint can prompt early rendering preparation, but it can also create a stacking context, containing block or extra graphics memory use.\n- **When not to:** Do not add the hint when a measured animation does not benefit from preparation.\n- **Pitfall:** Leaving `will-change: transform` on a permanent page shell can change fixed descendants and retain an unnecessary rendering layer.\n- **Support:** Baseline widely available since 2022-07-15 (web-features `will-change`). Chrome 36 / Firefox 36 / Safari 9.1.\n- **See also:** [MDN: CSS will-change](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/will-change)\n\n### P10. Main-thread long tasks\n\n- **Rule:** Split, move or yield work that blocks the main thread for more than 50 milliseconds.\n- **Why:** A long task delays input and rendering until the browser can run another task.\n- **When not to:** Keep a bounded task together when it completes below the long-task threshold and does not delay an interaction.\n- **Pitfall:** A third-party script can block input even when the app's own handlers are short.\n- **Support:** Judgment, no version gate.\n- **See also:** [web.dev: Optimize long tasks](https://web.dev/articles/optimize-long-tasks)\n\n---\n\n## 5. RESPONSIVE IMAGE DELIVERY\n\n### P8. srcset and sizes selection\n\n- **Rule:** Describe the image's rendered width in `sizes` when `srcset` uses width descriptors.\n- **Why:** The browser multiplies the selected slot width by device pixel ratio to choose a source candidate. A 600-pixel slot at DPR 2 needs a candidate near 1200 pixels.\n- **When not to:** Use density descriptors when the source set represents the same rendered dimensions at different pixel densities.\n- **Pitfall:** Setting `sizes=\"100vw\"` for a 600-pixel column can select a much larger image than the layout needs.\n- **Support:** Baseline widely available since 2019-09-27 (web-features `srcset`). Chrome 38 / Firefox 38 / Safari 10.1. Baseline widely available since 2019-09-27 (web-features `srcset`). Chrome 38 / Firefox 38 / Safari 10.1.\n- **See also:** [MDN: Responsive images](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Guides/Responsive_images)\n\n### P9. Picture formats and image hints\n\n- **Rule:** List preferred AVIF and WebP sources before the JPEG `<img>` fallback, use loading, decoding and priority hints for their intended stages, and use `sizes=\"auto\"` only as an enhancement.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"router_state: active\nskill_pointer: SKILL.md\n---\n\n# Frontend Surface Router\n\nThe machine router for [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md). The core reference is the default resource; each intent adds the web layer or Figma check it needs.\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThis surface holds the core in `references/frontend-practice.md`, the web layer in `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, six web topic files, and the five-pass Figma check in `references/figma-to-code.md`. Every intent loads the core and the matching web or Figma-to-code layer. Topic files load when the request touches their listed concern.\n\n### Web Topic Files\n\n| Topic | File | Load when |\n|---|---|---|\n| Elements and attributes | [web-elements-and-attributes.md](references/web-elements-and-attributes.md) | Adding or changing a dialog, popover, disclosure, form-control attribute, or resource hint |\n| Cascade and selectors | [web-cascade-and-selectors.md](references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md) | Changing selector reach, cascade layers, specificity, or component style boundaries |\n| Layout and sizing | [web-layout-and-sizing.md](references/web-layout-and-sizing.md) | Changing stacking, containing blocks, intrinsic sizing, container queries, or scrolling |\n===FIGMA 13-40===\n# Figma to Code Translation\n\nHow to read a Figma design as a reference and build the simplest correct structure from it.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Core Principle\n\nFigma is a reference for code, never its markup. Never copy the layer tree, absolute coordinates, fixed frame sizes or component property sets 1:1 into code.\n\n### Purpose\n\nA Figma read, export or MCP pull tells you what the screen should look like and which states it has. It does not tell you which elements to write.\n\n### When to Use\n\n- Reading a Figma frame before writing code\n- Translating auto layout, sizing or absolute layers into CSS\n- Mapping Figma variables and styles to installed tokens\n- Running the five-pass check against a rendered build\n- Reporting a Figma-to-code red flag\n\n### Boundaries\n\nThis file does not own:\n\n===I18N 105-125===\n### I7. Date-only parsing\n\n- **Rule:** Parse date-only values as calendar dates in the intended locale and time zone instead of converting them through UTC timestamps.\n- **Why:** JavaScript parses an ISO date-only string such as `2026-11-02` at UTC midnight, which can display as the previous local date in a negative offset.\n- **When not to:** Use a timestamp when the input represents an exact instant rather than a calendar date.\n- **Pitfall:** Calling `toISOString().slice(0, 10)` on a local date can serialize a different calendar day.\n- **Support:** Judgment, no version gate.\n- **See also:** [MDN: Date.parse()](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Date/parse)\n\n---\n\n## 5. TRANSLATION-TOLERANT TEXT\n\n### I9. Expansion and pseudo-localization\n\n- **Rule:** Test layouts with pseudo-localized text and leave room for German and Dutch strings that can grow by about 30 to 35 percent.\n- **Why:** Translation changes word length and line breaks, which can push fixed-width controls past their available space.\n- **When not to:** Use a fixed measure only when the content has a documented hard limit, such as a machine identifier.\n- **Pitfall:** A button that fits the source language can clip its translated label when its width is fixed.\n- **Support:** Judgment, no version gate.\n- **See also:** [MDN: Localization and plurals](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Localization/Localization_and_Plurals)\n===PERF 105-135===\n- **Why:** The hint can prompt early rendering preparation, but it can also create a stacking context, containing block or extra graphics memory use.\n- **When not to:** Do not add the hint when a measured animation does not benefit from preparation.\n- **Pitfall:** Leaving `will-change: transform` on a permanent page shell can change fixed descendants and retain an unnecessary rendering layer.\n- **Support:** Baseline widely available since 2022-07-15 (web-features `will-change`). Chrome 36 / Firefox 36 / Safari 9.1.\n- **See also:** [MDN: CSS will-change](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/will-change)\n\n### P10. Main-thread long tasks\n\n- **Rule:** Split, move or yield work that blocks the main thread for more than 50 milliseconds.\n- **Why:** A long task delays input and rendering until the browser can run another task.\n- **When not to:** Keep a bounded task together when it completes below the long-task threshold and does not delay an interaction.\n- **Pitfall:** A third-party script can block input even when the app's own handlers are short.\n- **Support:** Judgment, no version gate.\n- **See also:** [web.dev: Optimize long tasks](https://web.dev/articles/optimize-long-tasks)\n\n---\n\n## 5. RESPONSIVE IMAGE DELIVERY\n\n### P8. srcset and sizes selection\n\n- **Rule:** Describe the image's rendered width in `sizes` when `srcset` uses width descriptors.\n- **Why:** The browser multiplies the selected slot width by device pixel ratio to choose a source candidate. A 600-pixel slot at DPR 2 needs a candidate near 1200 pixels.\n- **When not to:** Use density descriptors when the source set represents the same rendered dimensions at different pixel densities.\n- **Pitfall:** Setting `sizes=\"100vw\"` for a 600-pixel column can select a much larger image than the layout needs.\n- **Support:** Baseline widely available since 2019-09-27 (web-features `srcset`). Chrome 38 / Firefox 38 / Safari 10.1. Baseline widely available since 2019-09-27 (web-features `srcset`). Chrome 38 / Firefox 38 / Safari 10.1.\n- **See also:** [MDN: Responsive images](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Guides/Responsive_images)\n\n### P9. Picture formats and image hints\n\n- **Rule:** List preferred AVIF and WebP sources before the JPEG `<img>` fallback, use loading, decoding and priority hints for their intended stages, and use `sizes=\"auto\"` only as an enhancement.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"sed -n '10,28p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md; echo \\\"===FIGMA 13-40===\\\"; sed -n '13,40p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/figma-to-code.md; echo \\\"===I18N 105-125===\\\"; sed -n '105,125p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-internationalization.md; echo \\\"===PERF 105-135===\\\"; sed -n '105,135p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793742659214,"end":1793742659391}}}}
