{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793742667448,"sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","part":{"id":"prt_1a364feb8001Adac5qoSdV4A91","sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","messageID":"msg_1a364f570001zWImQMyA1Z4rB3","type":"step-start","snapshot":"f51c493a61e015dd34511c34cd94b1ede1a58f61"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793742679717,"sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","part":{"partID":"prt_1a3652cb60016eHtvXBkrD86qh","sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","messageID":"msg_1a364f570001zWImQMyA1Z4rB3","type":"tool","id":"call_00_gn2e1i806u00y7p0pxf3c6ys","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 3: sk-code-frontend References and the Pre-Fix Cascade File\n\n## Focus\n\nAudit `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/` references against the enumerated defect classes, using the pre-fix `web-cascade-and-selectors.md` at commit `cd00629166` as the known-bad control and the current HEAD file as the remediation control.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read the heading map of all ten frontend references plus `SKILL.md` and `ROUTER.md`.\n2. Read the pre-fix `web-cascade-and-selectors.md` extracted from commit `cd00629166` and diffed it against HEAD.\n3. Read the current `web-cascade-and-selectors.md`, `figma-to-code.md` overview, `web-internationalization.md` §4-§5 and `web-performance-and-loading.md` §4-§5.\n4. Grepped the pre-fix copy for adjacent bold labels, bare URLs and duplicate labels to get exact lines.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The pre-fix `web-cascade-and-selectors.md` carries the consecutive-bold-label defect on every rule: lines 23-28 are six adjacent `**Rule.**` / `**Why.**` / `**When not to.**` / `**Pitfall.**` / `**Support.**` / `**See also.**` lines with no blank lines, so CommonMark joins them into one paragraph and the label structure disappears in the rendered page. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md:23 (at cd00629166)]\n\n2. The same pre-fix file opens with `## 1. OVERVIEW AND CASCADE AND SPECIFICITY` and then goes directly to `### CS1. Cascade decision order`, so the section that promises an overview contains no overview, no Purpose and no When to Use. This is exactly the \"OVERVIEW AND <topic>\" accretion pattern named in the brief. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md:19 (at cd00629166)]\n\n3. The pre-fix file has nine bare URLs, one per rule, each placed after a `**See also.**` label and never wrapped in a link: lines 28, 37, 46, 60, 69, 82, 91, 100 and 109. It also repeats the same `**Support.**` line twice inside CS4 at lines 58-59, so the reader sees the same compatibility sentence twice with no explanation. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md:28 (at cd00629166)] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md:58 (at cd00629166)]\n\n4. The current HEAD version fixes the shape by converting each rule block to a bullet list and each bare URL to a named link, which confirms the intended remediation: `- **Rule:**` ... `- **See also:** [MDN: CSS cascade](...)`. The fix is real, but it was applied to this file rather than enforced, so the class survives elsewhere. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md:41] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md:48]\n\n5. `web-performance-and-loading.md` orders rule ids by authoring history rather than reader task: §4 ends with `### P10. Main-thread long tasks` at line 111, then §5 begins with `### P8. srcset and sizes selection` at 124 and `### P9. Picture formats and image hints` at 133. A reader following the ids meets P10 before P8 and P9, and the section boundary hides the inversion. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md:111] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md:124] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md:133]\n\n6. The duplicate-label class the pre-fix file showed also survives at HEAD: `web-performance-and-loading.md` P8 repeats the entire support sentence twice in one bullet, \"Baseline widely available since 2019-09-27 (web-features `srcset`). Chrome 38 / Firefox 38 / Safari 10.1.\" followed by the same sentence again. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md:130]\n\n7. `web-internationalization.md` jumps from `### I7. Date-only parsing` (105) to `### I9. Expansion and pseudo-localization` (118) with no I8 anywhere in the file, so the numbering records a deleted or moved rule and gives the reader a false sense that a rule is missing. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-internationalization.md:105] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-internationalization.md:118]\n\n8. `figma-to-code.md` is the only web-family reference whose OVERVIEW starts with `### Core Principle` (21) before `### Purpose` (25) and `### When to Use` (29); every sibling `web-*.md` starts with Purpose, When to Use, Boundaries. The same packet therefore presents two overview orders. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/figma-to-code.md:21] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/figma-to-code.md:25] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md:21]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Treating the current `web-cascade-and-selectors.md` as still defective: the diff shows the bold-label blocks became bullet lists and the bare URLs became named links, so the file now matches the template shape.\n- Treating `frontend-practice.md:95` and `:102` (`**Layers**`, `**Web topic files**`) as adjacent bold joins: they are separated by blank lines and body text, so they render as separate label paragraphs.\n- Treating the `**Deeper:**` handoff lines in `web-markup-and-css.md` as orphaned labels: each closes a section with a valid link.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Searching for current bare URLs in the frontend references: all nine were repaired in the restructure, so the class is now historical in this family but live elsewhere.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: the pre-fix file no longer exists at HEAD, so its line citations are commit-relative and labelled `(at cd00629166)`.\n- Contradictory evidence: HEAD passes the shape checks while the pre-fix commit failed them, so the same path yields two different verdicts depending on revision; the finding records the revision.\n- Missing dependencies: none.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md` (HEAD)\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md` at `cd00629166`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md:105-144`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-internationalization.md:105-125`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/figma-to-code.md:13-40`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md:13-69`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md:10-28`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.75\n- Questions addressed: frontend reference defects, including the pre-fix control.\n- Questions answered: \"Which sk-code-frontend references, including web-cascade-and-selectors.md, carry the enumerated rendering defects, and at which exact lines?\"\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: diffing the pre-fix commit against HEAD produced a precise remediated shape, which made the surviving duplicate-support and id-order defects obvious by contrast.\n- What did not work and why: the current-file structural scan reported zero bold-join and zero bare-URL hits, because the restructure repaired this family; without the commit control the audit would have under-reported the class.\n- What I would do differently: pull the pre-fix control before scanning any family, since a clean current file does not prove the class is absent from the corpus or the validator.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nIteration 4: `sk-code-quality` references, where the first iteration already flagged `runner-contract.md` as an OVERVIEW with no overview and the longest introduction in the corpus.\n","path":"specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 3: sk-code-frontend References and the Pre-Fix Cascade File\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nAudit `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/` references against the enumerated defect classes, using the pre-fix `web-cascade-and-selectors.md` at commit `cd00629166` as the known-bad control and the current HEAD file as the remediation control.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Read the heading map of all ten frontend references plus `SKILL.md` and `ROUTER.md`.\\n2. Read the pre-fix `web-cascade-and-selectors.md` extracted from commit `cd00629166` and diffed it against HEAD.\\n3. Read the current `web-cascade-and-selectors.md`, `figma-to-code.md` overview, `web-internationalization.md` §4-§5 and `web-performance-and-loading.md` §4-§5.\\n4. Grepped the pre-fix copy for adjacent bold labels, bare URLs and duplicate labels to get exact lines.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. The pre-fix `web-cascade-and-selectors.md` carries the consecutive-bold-label defect on every rule: lines 23-28 are six adjacent `**Rule.**` / `**Why.**` / `**When not to.**` / `**Pitfall.**` / `**Support.**` / `**See also.**` lines with no blank lines, so CommonMark joins them into one paragraph and the label structure disappears in the rendered page. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md:23 (at cd00629166)]\\n\\n2. The same pre-fix file opens with `## 1. OVERVIEW AND CASCADE AND SPECIFICITY` and then goes directly to `### CS1. Cascade decision order`, so the section that promises an overview contains no overview, no Purpose and no When to Use. This is exactly the \\\"OVERVIEW AND <topic>\\\" accretion pattern named in the brief. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md:19 (at cd00629166)]\\n\\n3. The pre-fix file has nine bare URLs, one per rule, each placed after a `**See also.**` label and never wrapped in a link: lines 28, 37, 46, 60, 69, 82, 91, 100 and 109. It also repeats the same `**Support.**` line twice inside CS4 at lines 58-59, so the reader sees the same compatibility sentence twice with no explanation. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md:28 (at cd00629166)] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md:58 (at cd00629166)]\\n\\n4. The current HEAD version fixes the shape by converting each rule block to a bullet list and each bare URL to a named link, which confirms the intended remediation: `- **Rule:**` ... `- **See also:** [MDN: CSS cascade](...)`. The fix is real, but it was applied to this file rather than enforced, so the class survives elsewhere. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md:41] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md:48]\\n\\n5. `web-performance-and-loading.md` orders rule ids by authoring history rather than reader task: §4 ends with `### P10. Main-thread long tasks` at line 111, then §5 begins with `### P8. srcset and sizes selection` at 124 and `### P9. Picture formats and image hints` at 133. A reader following the ids meets P10 before P8 and P9, and the section boundary hides the inversion. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md:111] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md:124] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md:133]\\n\\n6. The duplicate-label class the pre-fix file showed also survives at HEAD: `web-performance-and-loading.md` P8 repeats the entire support sentence twice in one bullet, \\\"Baseline widely available since 2019-09-27 (web-features `srcset`). Chrome 38 / Firefox 38 / Safari 10.1.\\\" followed by the same sentence again. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md:130]\\n\\n7. `web-internationalization.md` jumps from `### I7. Date-only parsing` (105) to `### I9. Expansion and pseudo-localization` (118) with no I8 anywhere in the file, so the numbering records a deleted or moved rule and gives the reader a false sense that a rule is missing. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-internationalization.md:105] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-internationalization.md:118]\\n\\n8. `figma-to-code.md` is the only web-family reference whose OVERVIEW starts with `### Core Principle` (21) before `### Purpose` (25) and `### When to Use` (29); every sibling `web-*.md` starts with Purpose, When to Use, Boundaries. The same packet therefore presents two overview orders. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/figma-to-code.md:21] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/figma-to-code.md:25] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md:21]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Treating the current `web-cascade-and-selectors.md` as still defective: the diff shows the bold-label blocks became bullet lists and the bare URLs became named links, so the file now matches the template shape.\\n- Treating `frontend-practice.md:95` and `:102` (`**Layers**`, `**Web topic files**`) as adjacent bold joins: they are separated by blank lines and body text, so they render as separate label paragraphs.\\n- Treating the `**Deeper:**` handoff lines in `web-markup-and-css.md` as orphaned labels: each closes a section with a valid link.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Searching for current bare URLs in the frontend references: all nine were repaired in the restructure, so the class is now historical in this family but live elsewhere.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: the pre-fix file no longer exists at HEAD, so its line citations are commit-relative and labelled `(at cd00629166)`.\\n- Contradictory evidence: HEAD passes the shape checks while the pre-fix commit failed them, so the same path yields two different verdicts depending on revision; the finding records the revision.\\n- Missing dependencies: none.\\n- Partial success: none.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md` (HEAD)\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md` at `cd00629166`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md:105-144`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-internationalization.md:105-125`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/figma-to-code.md:13-40`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md:13-69`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md:10-28`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.75\\n- Questions addressed: frontend reference defects, including the pre-fix control.\\n- Questions answered: \\\"Which sk-code-frontend references, including web-cascade-and-selectors.md, carry the enumerated rendering defects, and at which exact lines?\\\"\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: diffing the pre-fix commit against HEAD produced a precise remediated shape, which made the surviving duplicate-support and id-order defects obvious by contrast.\\n- What did not work and why: the current-file structural scan reported zero bold-join and zero bare-URL hits, because the restructure repaired this family; without the commit control the audit would have under-reported the class.\\n- What I would do differently: pull the pre-fix control before scanning any family, since a clean current file does not prove the class is absent from the corpus or the validator.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nIteration 4: `sk-code-quality` references, where the first iteration already flagged `runner-contract.md` as an OVERVIEW with no overview and the longest introduction in the corpus.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793742679222,"end":1793742679717}}}}
