{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793742771099,"sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","part":{"partID":"prt_1a366937a001AQSKaBdSK0j2tp","sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","messageID":"msg_1a3667ca1001w0cwsdWtCEFu5F","type":"tool","id":"call_00_bjnzswwd1ikhd26uvo3xbt6x","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/pr-state-dedup.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/pr-state-dedup.md, lines 1-99\n1: ---\n2: title: PR-State Content-Hash Dedup\n3: description: Signature computation, JSONL cache format, retention, and skip behavior for the M-1 PR-state review deduplication gate.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"pr state dedup gate\"\n6:   - \"review diff signature hash\"\n7:   - \"duplicate review skip behavior\"\n8:   - \"review dedup cache retention\"\n9:   - \"commented no changes status\"\n10: importance_tier: important\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 1.6.0.0\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # PR-State Content-Hash Dedup (M-1)\n16: \n17: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n18: \n19: Detailed reference for the M-1 PR-state deduplication gate documented in `../SKILL.md` §9.1.\n20: \n21: ## Signature Computation\n22: \n23: ```text\n24: diff_content_hash = sha256(git diff <base-ref>...HEAD)\n25: signature         = sha256(commit_subject + \"\\u001f\" + diff_content_hash)\n26: ```\n27: \n28: - `commit_subject`: first line of `git log <base-ref>...HEAD --format=%s` (latest commit subject only)\n29: - `diff_content_hash`: full diff content, not `--stat` or `--numstat`\n30: - Separator `\\u001f` (Unit Separator) prevents collision between subject and hash boundaries\n31: \n32: ### Example\n33: \n34: ```bash\n35: BASE=\"origin/main\"\n36: SCOPE=\"\"   # optional pathspec, such as packages/api; empty means the whole repository\n37: DIFF_HASH=$(git diff $BASE...HEAD ${SCOPE:+-- \"$SCOPE\"} | sha256sum | awk '{print $1}')\n38: SUBJECT=$(git log $BASE...HEAD --format=%s ${SCOPE:+-- \"$SCOPE\"} | head -1)\n39: SIGNATURE=$(printf '%s\\x1f%s' \"$SUBJECT\" \"$DIFF_HASH\" | sha256sum | awk '{print $1}')\n40: ```\n41: \n42: ## Cache Format\n43: \n44: **Path:** `${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/sk-code-review/<repo-ref>.jsonl`\n45: \n46: The cache lives in the reviewing user's cache directory, outside every reviewed repository. Its one side effect is this file. The gate never creates a file or folder in the repository it reviews.\n47: \n48: - `<repo-ref>` = `sha256(<repo identity>).slice(0, 12)`, where `<repo identity>` is the output of `git remote get-url origin`. When the repository has no `origin` remote, `<repo identity>` falls back to `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, the absolute path of the repository root, so a local-only repository still gets a stable key\n49: - With a pathspec scope, `<repo-ref>` = `sha256(<repo identity> + \"\\u001f\" + <pathspec>).slice(0, 12)`, so each scoped package keeps its own cache file\n50: - One JSON object per line (JSONL format)\n51: - File is append-only with periodic pruning\n52: \n53: **Schema per line:**\n54: \n55: ```json\n56: {\"signature\": \"<sha256-hex-64>\", \"timestamp\": \"<ISO-8601>\", \"prev_sha\": \"<full-commit-sha>\"}\n57: ```\n58: \n59: ## Pathspec Scope\n60: \n61: The scope is optional. With no pathspec, the whole repository is one scope, which is the behavior every earlier cache entry was written under.\n62: \n63: When a review targets one package of a monorepo, pass that package path as the pathspec. The same pathspec then goes to every command the gate runs:\n64: \n65: - `git diff <base-ref>...HEAD -- <pathspec>` for `diff_content_hash`\n66: - `git log <base-ref>...HEAD --format=%s -- <pathspec>` for `commit_subject`\n67: - the `<repo-ref>` hash above\n68: \n69: A change outside the package then leaves that package's signature unchanged, and a change inside it no longer matches a whole-repository entry.\n70: \n71: ## Retention\n72: \n73: - Maximum **100 entries** per repo-ref\n74: - On write: append, then if line count > 100, keep last 100 lines\n75: - No TTL-based expiry — entries persist until pruned by the 100-entry cap\n76: - Cache file may be deleted entirely to reset; recreated on next write\n77: \n78: ## Skip Behavior\n79: \n80: When a review is requested and the computed signature matches a prior cache entry:\n81: \n82: ```\n83: Review status: COMMENTED (no changes since last review at <prev_sha>)\n84: ```\n85: \n86: - No full review analysis is performed\n87: - The cached `prev_sha` is reported so operators can verify\n88: - Downstream automation must treat `COMMENTED` as equivalent to a pass (no new findings)\n89: \n90: ## Cache Write\n91: \n92: After every **full review** that reaches the final status line, write the current signature to cache. If the gate skipped the review (COMMENTED match), do NOT re-write — the existing cache entry remains authoritative.\n93: \n94: ## Cache Location Rationale\n95: \n96: - The user cache directory sits outside every reviewed repository, so reviewing a foreign repository leaves no folder in it, and deleting the cache folder resets the gate\n97: - `<repo-ref>` deduplication supports multiple remotes / forks without collision\n98: - JSONL format allows line-level append and simple head/tail operations for retention\n99: - The root-path fallback changes when the repository folder moves or is cloned to a new path. The worst case is one cache miss and one full review, never a skipped review","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/pr-state-dedup.md, lines 1-99\n1: ---\n2: title: PR-State Content-Hash Dedup\n3: description: Signature computation, JSONL cache format, retention, and skip behavior for the M-1 PR-state review deduplication gate.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"pr state dedup gate\"\n6:   - \"review diff signature hash\"\n7:   - \"duplicate review skip behavior\"\n8:   - \"review dedup cache retention\"\n9:   - \"commented no changes status\"\n10: importance_tier: important\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 1.6.0.0\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # PR-State Content-Hash Dedup (M-1)\n16: \n17: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n18: \n19: Detailed reference for the M-1 PR-state deduplication gate documented in `../SKILL.md` §9.1.\n20: \n21: ## Signature Computation\n22: \n23: ```text\n24: diff_content_hash = sha256(git diff <base-ref>...HEAD)\n25: signature         = sha256(commit_subject + \"\\u001f\" + diff_content_hash)\n26: ```\n27: \n28: - `commit_subject`: first line of `git log <base-ref>...HEAD --format=%s` (latest commit subject only)\n29: - `diff_content_hash`: full diff content, not `--stat` or `--numstat`\n30: - Separator `\\u001f` (Unit Separator) prevents collision between subject and hash boundaries\n31: \n32: ### Example\n33: \n34: ```bash\n35: BASE=\"origin/main\"\n36: SCOPE=\"\"   # optional pathspec, such as packages/api; empty means the whole repository\n37: DIFF_HASH=$(git diff $BASE...HEAD ${SCOPE:+-- \"$SCOPE\"} | sha256sum | awk '{print $1}')\n38: SUBJECT=$(git log $BASE...HEAD --format=%s ${SCOPE:+-- \"$SCOPE\"} | head -1)\n39: SIGNATURE=$(printf '%s\\x1f%s' \"$SUBJECT\" \"$DIFF_HASH\" | sha256sum | awk '{print $1}')\n40: ```\n41: \n42: ## Cache Format\n43: \n44: **Path:** `${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/sk-code-review/<repo-ref>.jsonl`\n45: \n46: The cache lives in the reviewing user's cache directory, outside every reviewed repository. Its one side effect is this file. The gate never creates a file or folder in the repository it reviews.\n47: \n48: - `<repo-ref>` = `sha256(<repo identity>).slice(0, 12)`, where `<repo identity>` is the output of `git remote get-url origin`. When the repository has no `origin` remote, `<repo identity>` falls back to `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, the absolute path of the repository root, so a local-only repository still gets a stable key\n49: - With a pathspec scope, `<repo-ref>` = `sha256(<repo identity> + \"\\u001f\" + <pathspec>).slice(0, 12)`, so each scoped package keeps its own cache file\n50: - One JSON object per line (JSONL format)\n51: - File is append-only with periodic pruning\n52: \n53: **Schema per line:**\n54: \n55: ```json\n56: {\"signature\": \"<sha256-hex-64>\", \"timestamp\": \"<ISO-8601>\", \"prev_sha\": \"<full-commit-sha>\"}\n57: ```\n58: \n59: ## Pathspec Scope\n60: \n61: The scope is optional. With no pathspec, the whole repository is one scope, which is the behavior every earlier cache entry was written under.\n62: \n63: When a review targets one package of a monorepo, pass that package path as the pathspec. The same pathspec then goes to every command the gate runs:\n64: \n65: - `git diff <base-ref>...HEAD -- <pathspec>` for `diff_content_hash`\n66: - `git log <base-ref>...HEAD --format=%s -- <pathspec>` for `commit_subject`\n67: - the `<repo-ref>` hash above\n68: \n69: A change outside the package then leaves that package's signature unchanged, and a change inside it no longer matches a whole-repository entry.\n70: \n71: ## Retention\n72: \n73: - Maximum **100 entries** per repo-ref\n74: - On write: append, then if line count > 100, keep last 100 lines\n75: - No TTL-based expiry — entries persist until pruned by the 100-entry cap\n76: - Cache file may be deleted entirely to reset; recreated on next write\n77: \n78: ## Skip Behavior\n79: \n80: When a review is requested and the computed signature matches a prior cache entry:\n81: \n82: ```\n83: Review status: COMMENTED (no changes since last review at <prev_sha>)\n84: ```\n85: \n86: - No full review analysis is performed\n87: - The cached `prev_sha` is reported so operators can verify\n88: - Downstream automation must treat `COMMENTED` as equivalent to a pass (no new findings)\n89: \n90: ## Cache Write\n91: \n92: After every **full review** that reaches the final status line, write the current signature to cache. If the gate skipped the review (COMMENTED match), do NOT re-write — the existing cache entry remains authoritative.\n93: \n94: ## Cache Location Rationale\n95: \n96: - The user cache directory sits outside every reviewed repository, so reviewing a foreign repository leaves no folder in it, and deleting the cache folder resets the gate\n97: - `<repo-ref>` deduplication supports multiple remotes / forks without collision\n98: - JSONL format allows line-level append and simple head/tail operations for retention\n99: - The root-path fallback changes when the repository folder moves or is cloned to a new path. The worst case is one cache miss and one full review, never a skipped review"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/pr-state-dedup.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793742771066,"end":1793742771099}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793742771101,"sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","part":{"partID":"prt_1a3669385001qMNeCva8tvOHju","sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","messageID":"msg_1a3667ca1001w0cwsdWtCEFu5F","type":"tool","id":"call_01_mexz42jn2td45zbhfhyoce26","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/quick-reference.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/quick-reference.md, lines 1-63\n1: ---\n2: title: Code Review Quick Reference\n3: description: Lightweight index for review core doctrine and single-pass review UX guidance.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"code review quick reference\"\n6:   - \"review reference map\"\n7:   - \"split review references index\"\n8:   - \"which review checklist to load\"\n9: importance_tier: normal\n10: contextType: general\n11: version: 1.5.1.0\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Code Review Quick Reference\n15: \n16: Lightweight index for the split review references in this skill.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: ### Purpose\n23: \n24: Route review consumers to the correct reference file based on their intent. This file replaces the former monolithic quick reference with a split architecture: shared doctrine in `review-core.md` and interactive UX rules in `review-ux-single-pass.md`.\n25: \n26: ### Usage\n27: \n28: Use this file as an entry index, not as the primary source of review rules. Load the specific reference that matches your mode:\n29: - **Both modes** (single-pass and deep review): Load `review-core.md`\n30: - **Interactive single-pass only**: Also load `review-ux-single-pass.md`\n31: - **Deep review only**: Core doctrine is loaded via the `@deep-review` agent contract\n32: \n33: ---\n34: \n35: ## 2. REFERENCE MAP\n36: \n37: | Reference | Scope | Consumers |\n38: |-----------|-------|-----------|\n39: | [review-core.md](./review-core.md) | Shared doctrine: severity, evidence, findings schema, baseline+surface precedence, floor and default lens ids, rule overrides and the `Rule sources:` line | `@review`, `@deep-review` |\n40: | [review-ux-single-pass.md](./review-ux-single-pass.md) | Interactive UX: report flow, next-step prompts, PR/pre-commit guidance | `@review` only |\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: ## 3. SUPPORTING CHECKLISTS\n45: \n46: | Checklist | Purpose |\n47: |-----------|---------|\n48: | [security-checklist.md](../assets/security-checklist.md) | Security, reliability, and abuse-prevention checks |\n49: | [code-quality-checklist.md](../assets/code-quality-checklist.md) | Non-security correctness, KISS, and DRY checks |\n50: | [solid-checklist.md](../assets/solid-checklist.md) | Architecture and SOLID (SRP/OCP/LSP/ISP/DIP) checks |\n51: | [removal-plan.md](../assets/removal-plan.md) | Safe-now versus deferred deletion planning |\n52: | [test-quality-checklist.md](../assets/test-quality-checklist.md) | Test quality, coverage, and anti-pattern detection |\n53: \n54: Surface portability: apply this baseline with `sk-code` surface evidence.\n55: \n56: ---\n57: \n58: ## 4. RELATED RESOURCES\n59: \n60: - [SKILL.md](../SKILL.md) - Parent skill definition with activation triggers and resource loading rules\n61: - [review-mode-contract.yaml](../../../system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml) - Deep-review contract manifest. It owns the deep-review loop and consumes the severity ids that [review-core.md](./review-core.md) owns. review-core.md wins when the two disagree on a severity id or its meaning\n62: \n63: ---","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/quick-reference.md, lines 1-63\n1: ---\n2: title: Code Review Quick Reference\n3: description: Lightweight index for review core doctrine and single-pass review UX guidance.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"code review quick reference\"\n6:   - \"review reference map\"\n7:   - \"split review references index\"\n8:   - \"which review checklist to load\"\n9: importance_tier: normal\n10: contextType: general\n11: version: 1.5.1.0\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Code Review Quick Reference\n15: \n16: Lightweight index for the split review references in this skill.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: ### Purpose\n23: \n24: Route review consumers to the correct reference file based on their intent. This file replaces the former monolithic quick reference with a split architecture: shared doctrine in `review-core.md` and interactive UX rules in `review-ux-single-pass.md`.\n25: \n26: ### Usage\n27: \n28: Use this file as an entry index, not as the primary source of review rules. Load the specific reference that matches your mode:\n29: - **Both modes** (single-pass and deep review): Load `review-core.md`\n30: - **Interactive single-pass only**: Also load `review-ux-single-pass.md`\n31: - **Deep review only**: Core doctrine is loaded via the `@deep-review` agent contract\n32: \n33: ---\n34: \n35: ## 2. REFERENCE MAP\n36: \n37: | Reference | Scope | Consumers |\n38: |-----------|-------|-----------|\n39: | [review-core.md](./review-core.md) | Shared doctrine: severity, evidence, findings schema, baseline+surface precedence, floor and default lens ids, rule overrides and the `Rule sources:` line | `@review`, `@deep-review` |\n40: | [review-ux-single-pass.md](./review-ux-single-pass.md) | Interactive UX: report flow, next-step prompts, PR/pre-commit guidance | `@review` only |\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: ## 3. SUPPORTING CHECKLISTS\n45: \n46: | Checklist | Purpose |\n47: |-----------|---------|\n48: | [security-checklist.md](../assets/security-checklist.md) | Security, reliability, and abuse-prevention checks |\n49: | [code-quality-checklist.md](../assets/code-quality-checklist.md) | Non-security correctness, KISS, and DRY checks |\n50: | [solid-checklist.md](../assets/solid-checklist.md) | Architecture and SOLID (SRP/OCP/LSP/ISP/DIP) checks |\n51: | [removal-plan.md](../assets/removal-plan.md) | Safe-now versus deferred deletion planning |\n52: | [test-quality-checklist.md](../assets/test-quality-checklist.md) | Test quality, coverage, and anti-pattern detection |\n53: \n54: Surface portability: apply this baseline with `sk-code` surface evidence.\n55: \n56: ---\n57: \n58: ## 4. RELATED RESOURCES\n59: \n60: - [SKILL.md](../SKILL.md) - Parent skill definition with activation triggers and resource loading rules\n61: - [review-mode-contract.yaml](../../../system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml) - Deep-review contract manifest. It owns the deep-review loop and consumes the severity ids that [review-core.md](./review-core.md) owns. review-core.md wins when the two disagree on a severity id or its meaning\n62: \n63: ---"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/quick-reference.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793742771077,"end":1793742771101}}}}
