{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793742787253,"sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","part":{"id":"prt_1a366d2b5001UA3xQgsHyINaNh","sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","messageID":"msg_1a366cbe0001mL0BE943VgypMI","type":"step-start","snapshot":"50d5a7dafcd96b9e2fd95a653ba504e9c53d9317"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793742796011,"sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","part":{"partID":"prt_1a366f331001bcRieR1BeZQDBL","sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","messageID":"msg_1a366cbe0001mL0BE943VgypMI","type":"tool","id":"call_00_6qgj88cgsnyrvwchzng93fes","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 5: sk-code-review References and Assets\n\n## Focus\n\nAudit `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/` — `SKILL.md`, `ROUTER.md`, four references and six checklist assets — for split link sections, mixed numbering, index omissions and missing closing sections.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read `pr-state-dedup.md` and `quick-reference.md` end to end.\n2. Extracted the heading map of `review-core.md`, `review-ux-single-pass.md` and the six assets.\n3. Read `SKILL.md` §5-§9 to compare its two link sections and the position of the related section.\n4. Read the tails of the three checklists that appeared to lack a closing section, to avoid a false omission finding.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. `SKILL.md` carries two separate link inventories and puts the related section before live content: `## 5. REFERENCES` at 262 lists ten files, `## 8. RELATED RESOURCES` at 324 lists a second entry path, and `## 9. PR-STATE EFFICIENCY GATES` at 342 follows the related section. A reader looking for the PR-state gate is sent past the \"related resources\" close, and the same file list appears twice. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md:262] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md:324] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md:342]\n\n2. `pr-state-dedup.md` mixes one numbered section with a run of unnumbered peers: `## 1. OVERVIEW` at 17 is followed by `## Signature Computation` (21), `## Cache Format` (42), `## Pathspec Scope` (59), `## Retention` (71), `## Skip Behavior` (78), `## Cache Write` (90) and `## Cache Location Rationale` (94). The document implies a numbered structure and then abandons it after the first section. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/pr-state-dedup.md:17] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/pr-state-dedup.md:21] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/pr-state-dedup.md:42]\n\n3. `quick-reference.md`'s `## 3. SUPPORTING CHECKLISTS` table lists five checklists but omits `fix-completeness-checklist.md`, which exists in `assets/` and is listed in `SKILL.md` §5. The index that promises to route consumers to the correct checklist therefore cannot route them to the fix-completeness one. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/quick-reference.md:44] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/quick-reference.md:48] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md:272]\n\n4. `pr-state-dedup.md` ends on `## Cache Location Rationale` (94) with no Related Resources section, even though it is the reference `SKILL.md` §9.1 points at; the reader reaches the last bullet with no link back to `review-core.md` or `quick-reference.md`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/pr-state-dedup.md:94] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md:342]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Claiming the three checklist assets lack a closing related section: their tails carry link lists under a related heading, so the omission is specific to `pr-state-dedup.md`.\n- Treating `review-core.md` §9's long Python resolver as misplaced: it is an executable contract the section names, not unrelated prose.\n- Treating `quick-reference.md`'s `### Usage` heading as a template violation on its own: the deeper defect is the incomplete table, not the heading name.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Looking for adjacent bold labels in the review references: the packet uses bullets and tables, so the class is absent here.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: `SKILL.md` §5 and §8 could be read as \"core references\" versus \"related resources\"; the finding only claims the duplication and the placement before §9, not that either section is redundant on its own.\n- Contradictory evidence: `quick-reference.md` claims to be the routing index while `SKILL.md` §5 is the fuller list, so the two indexes disagree on coverage.\n- Missing dependencies: none.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md:255-419`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/pr-state-dedup.md:1-99`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/quick-reference.md:1-63`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/review-core.md:16-405`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/assets/*.md` heading maps and tails\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.80\n- Questions addressed: review reference and asset structure, index completeness, closing sections.\n- Questions answered: \"Which sk-code-review references and assets carry the enumerated rendering defects or structural divergence, and at which exact lines?\"\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: comparing the index table against the assets directory found an omission a heading scan cannot see, because the omitted file has no row to inspect.\n- What did not work and why: the first pass suspected three assets of missing related sections; reading their tails showed link lists under a heading the truncated map had hidden, so the claim was narrowed to one file.\n- What I would do differently: diff every index table against `ls` of the directory it claims to index, in every family.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nIteration 6: `sk-code-skilled`, the largest family (~45 references and ~20 checklist assets), to test whether the defects are systematic across a file family.\n","path":"specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 5: sk-code-review References and Assets\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nAudit `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/` — `SKILL.md`, `ROUTER.md`, four references and six checklist assets — for split link sections, mixed numbering, index omissions and missing closing sections.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Read `pr-state-dedup.md` and `quick-reference.md` end to end.\\n2. Extracted the heading map of `review-core.md`, `review-ux-single-pass.md` and the six assets.\\n3. Read `SKILL.md` §5-§9 to compare its two link sections and the position of the related section.\\n4. Read the tails of the three checklists that appeared to lack a closing section, to avoid a false omission finding.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. `SKILL.md` carries two separate link inventories and puts the related section before live content: `## 5. REFERENCES` at 262 lists ten files, `## 8. RELATED RESOURCES` at 324 lists a second entry path, and `## 9. PR-STATE EFFICIENCY GATES` at 342 follows the related section. A reader looking for the PR-state gate is sent past the \\\"related resources\\\" close, and the same file list appears twice. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md:262] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md:324] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md:342]\\n\\n2. `pr-state-dedup.md` mixes one numbered section with a run of unnumbered peers: `## 1. OVERVIEW` at 17 is followed by `## Signature Computation` (21), `## Cache Format` (42), `## Pathspec Scope` (59), `## Retention` (71), `## Skip Behavior` (78), `## Cache Write` (90) and `## Cache Location Rationale` (94). The document implies a numbered structure and then abandons it after the first section. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/pr-state-dedup.md:17] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/pr-state-dedup.md:21] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/pr-state-dedup.md:42]\\n\\n3. `quick-reference.md`'s `## 3. SUPPORTING CHECKLISTS` table lists five checklists but omits `fix-completeness-checklist.md`, which exists in `assets/` and is listed in `SKILL.md` §5. The index that promises to route consumers to the correct checklist therefore cannot route them to the fix-completeness one. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/quick-reference.md:44] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/quick-reference.md:48] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md:272]\\n\\n4. `pr-state-dedup.md` ends on `## Cache Location Rationale` (94) with no Related Resources section, even though it is the reference `SKILL.md` §9.1 points at; the reader reaches the last bullet with no link back to `review-core.md` or `quick-reference.md`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/pr-state-dedup.md:94] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md:342]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Claiming the three checklist assets lack a closing related section: their tails carry link lists under a related heading, so the omission is specific to `pr-state-dedup.md`.\\n- Treating `review-core.md` §9's long Python resolver as misplaced: it is an executable contract the section names, not unrelated prose.\\n- Treating `quick-reference.md`'s `### Usage` heading as a template violation on its own: the deeper defect is the incomplete table, not the heading name.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Looking for adjacent bold labels in the review references: the packet uses bullets and tables, so the class is absent here.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: `SKILL.md` §5 and §8 could be read as \\\"core references\\\" versus \\\"related resources\\\"; the finding only claims the duplication and the placement before §9, not that either section is redundant on its own.\\n- Contradictory evidence: `quick-reference.md` claims to be the routing index while `SKILL.md` §5 is the fuller list, so the two indexes disagree on coverage.\\n- Missing dependencies: none.\\n- Partial success: none.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md:255-419`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/pr-state-dedup.md:1-99`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/quick-reference.md:1-63`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/review-core.md:16-405`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/assets/*.md` heading maps and tails\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.80\\n- Questions addressed: review reference and asset structure, index completeness, closing sections.\\n- Questions answered: \\\"Which sk-code-review references and assets carry the enumerated rendering defects or structural divergence, and at which exact lines?\\\"\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: comparing the index table against the assets directory found an omission a heading scan cannot see, because the omitted file has no row to inspect.\\n- What did not work and why: the first pass suspected three assets of missing related sections; reading their tails showed link lists under a heading the truncated map had hidden, so the claim was narrowed to one file.\\n- What I would do differently: diff every index table against `ls` of the directory it claims to index, in every family.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nIteration 6: `sk-code-skilled`, the largest family (~45 references and ~20 checklist assets), to test whether the defects are systematic across a file family.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793742795569,"end":1793742796011}}}}
