{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793742819965,"sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","part":{"partID":"prt_1a367513b001CNxcUUPDOOEgGI","sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","messageID":"msg_1a3673a78001DbsnDgL6EJzemy","type":"tool","id":"call_00_mhae9mirgk674kws5zl5woxl","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '195,270p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/javascript/quality-standards/security-testing-and-exemptions.md; echo \"===ALIGN 130-160===\"; sed -n '130,160p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/shared/alignment-verification-automation.md"},"output":"const posts = await fetchUserPosts(user.id);\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. TEST FILE EXEMPTION TIER\n\nCLI-only test runners, setup scripts, and similar utilities are exempt from certain quality standards because they are executed directly (not imported as modules) and serve a different purpose than library code.\n\n### Scope\n\nThis exemption applies to:\n- Files in `scripts/tests/`\n- Files in `scripts/setup/`\n- Any file with a test runner shebang (e.g., `#!/usr/bin/env node`)\n\n### Exempted Standards\n\n| Standard                           | Reason for Exemption                                           |\n|------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|\n| `module.exports` requirement       | Test runners are executed directly, not imported by other code |\n| Guard clause requirement           | Scripts run once at CLI level; input validation is minimal     |\n| `[module-name]` error prefix       | Test output uses its own format (e.g., pass/fail assertions)   |\n\n### What Still Applies\n\nAll other quality standards remain in effect for test files, including:\n- `'use strict'` directive\n- JSDoc documentation for non-trivial functions\n- Error handling with try-catch for async operations\n- Security patterns (path traversal, input limits) if handling external input\n\n### Example\n\n```javascript\n#!/usr/bin/env node\n'use strict';\n\nconst assert = require('assert');\nconst { loadConfig } = require('../core/config');\n\n// No module.exports needed — this file is executed directly\n// No guard clauses needed — CLI-level script\n// No [module-name] prefix needed — test output format\n\nconst config = loadConfig('./fixtures/valid.yaml');\nassert.ok(config, 'Config should load successfully');\nassert.strictEqual(config.version, '1.0.0');\n\nconsole.log('PASS: All config tests passed');\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. SKILLED PLUGIN EXEMPTION TIER\n\nOpenCode plugin entrypoints and helper modules are exempt from the CommonJS export standard because the OpenCode plugin loader requires ESM default exports. This exemption is narrow and does not relax other JavaScript quality standards.\n\n### Scope\n\nThis exemption applies to:\n- `.opencode/plugins/*.{js,mjs,ts}`\n\n### Exempted Standards\n\n| Standard                           | Reason for Exemption                                                               |\n|------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| `module.exports` requirement       | OpenCode plugin loader requires ESM default export per `@opencode-ai/plugin/dist/index.d.ts` |\n\n### What Still Applies\n\nAll other quality standards remain in effect for OpenCode plugin files, including:\n- JSDoc on exports\n- Guard clauses\n- Security patterns\n- Error handling\n===ALIGN 130-160===\n- `--root` is repeatable; when omitted, current directory is scanned.\n- Files are deduplicated by realpath when repeated/overlapping roots are provided.\n- Output includes both rule id and severity (`[RULE] [ERROR|WARN]`).\n- Exit code `0` means no blocking findings (warnings are non-blocking by default).\n- Exit code `1` means one or more errors were found, or warnings were found with `--fail-on-warn`.\n- `--check-router` (default off) emits `ROUTER-DEAD-PATH` (ERROR) for any RESOURCE_MAP leaf with no file on disk. It also emits `ROUTER-DUAL-DECLARATION` (ERROR) when both `SKILL.md` and `ROUTER.md` declare a router, and that finding suppresses the dead-path leg for the skill: with two declarations neither document is read. Without the flag the router table is never parsed, so the default invocation is behavior-identical to omitting it.\n\n---\n\n## 5. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- [code-organization/overview-and-module-organization.md](code-organization/overview-and-module-organization.md)\n- [universal-patterns/naming-and-commenting.md](universal-patterns/naming-and-commenting.md)\n- [hooks.md](./hooks.md)\n- Drift-guard entry point: `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/scripts/run-all-drift-guards.sh` — runs this verifier, `verify_stack_folders.py`, `verify-router-sync.cjs` (every leg: 1a, 1b, 2, 3 and 4) and `verify-doc-claims.cjs` together as one gate.\n\n---\n\n## 6. ALIGNMENT AUTHORITY INTERFACE (sk-code-skilled)\n\nsk-code-skilled has exactly one alignment source of truth: the three-part interface\nbelow. Later coverage and activation work must consume this interface rather than\nre-derive a second RESOURCE_MAP parser or a local eligibility map.\n\n1. **Doc pointer.** This file plus the sk-code-skilled `SKILL.md` SMART ROUTING\n   block, which record that the `sk-code-router-sync.vitest.ts` suite was\n   retired, that `verify-router-sync.cjs` restores its checks, and what covers\n   each (section 3, \"Router-sync guard\"). The markdown-blind\n   `verify_alignment_drift.py` is not that authority.\n2. **Bijection module.** `qualifiedIdToLeaf` in\n   `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/lib/leaf-resource-contract.cjs`\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"const posts = await fetchUserPosts(user.id);\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. TEST FILE EXEMPTION TIER\n\nCLI-only test runners, setup scripts, and similar utilities are exempt from certain quality standards because they are executed directly (not imported as modules) and serve a different purpose than library code.\n\n### Scope\n\nThis exemption applies to:\n- Files in `scripts/tests/`\n- Files in `scripts/setup/`\n- Any file with a test runner shebang (e.g., `#!/usr/bin/env node`)\n\n### Exempted Standards\n\n| Standard                           | Reason for Exemption                                           |\n|------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|\n| `module.exports` requirement       | Test runners are executed directly, not imported by other code |\n| Guard clause requirement           | Scripts run once at CLI level; input validation is minimal     |\n| `[module-name]` error prefix       | Test output uses its own format (e.g., pass/fail assertions)   |\n\n### What Still Applies\n\nAll other quality standards remain in effect for test files, including:\n- `'use strict'` directive\n- JSDoc documentation for non-trivial functions\n- Error handling with try-catch for async operations\n- Security patterns (path traversal, input limits) if handling external input\n\n### Example\n\n```javascript\n#!/usr/bin/env node\n'use strict';\n\nconst assert = require('assert');\nconst { loadConfig } = require('../core/config');\n\n// No module.exports needed — this file is executed directly\n// No guard clauses needed — CLI-level script\n// No [module-name] prefix needed — test output format\n\nconst config = loadConfig('./fixtures/valid.yaml');\nassert.ok(config, 'Config should load successfully');\nassert.strictEqual(config.version, '1.0.0');\n\nconsole.log('PASS: All config tests passed');\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. SKILLED PLUGIN EXEMPTION TIER\n\nOpenCode plugin entrypoints and helper modules are exempt from the CommonJS export standard because the OpenCode plugin loader requires ESM default exports. This exemption is narrow and does not relax other JavaScript quality standards.\n\n### Scope\n\nThis exemption applies to:\n- `.opencode/plugins/*.{js,mjs,ts}`\n\n### Exempted Standards\n\n| Standard                           | Reason for Exemption                                                               |\n|------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| `module.exports` requirement       | OpenCode plugin loader requires ESM default export per `@opencode-ai/plugin/dist/index.d.ts` |\n\n### What Still Applies\n\nAll other quality standards remain in effect for OpenCode plugin files, including:\n- JSDoc on exports\n- Guard clauses\n- Security patterns\n- Error handling\n===ALIGN 130-160===\n- `--root` is repeatable; when omitted, current directory is scanned.\n- Files are deduplicated by realpath when repeated/overlapping roots are provided.\n- Output includes both rule id and severity (`[RULE] [ERROR|WARN]`).\n- Exit code `0` means no blocking findings (warnings are non-blocking by default).\n- Exit code `1` means one or more errors were found, or warnings were found with `--fail-on-warn`.\n- `--check-router` (default off) emits `ROUTER-DEAD-PATH` (ERROR) for any RESOURCE_MAP leaf with no file on disk. It also emits `ROUTER-DUAL-DECLARATION` (ERROR) when both `SKILL.md` and `ROUTER.md` declare a router, and that finding suppresses the dead-path leg for the skill: with two declarations neither document is read. Without the flag the router table is never parsed, so the default invocation is behavior-identical to omitting it.\n\n---\n\n## 5. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- [code-organization/overview-and-module-organization.md](code-organization/overview-and-module-organization.md)\n- [universal-patterns/naming-and-commenting.md](universal-patterns/naming-and-commenting.md)\n- [hooks.md](./hooks.md)\n- Drift-guard entry point: `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/scripts/run-all-drift-guards.sh` — runs this verifier, `verify_stack_folders.py`, `verify-router-sync.cjs` (every leg: 1a, 1b, 2, 3 and 4) and `verify-doc-claims.cjs` together as one gate.\n\n---\n\n## 6. ALIGNMENT AUTHORITY INTERFACE (sk-code-skilled)\n\nsk-code-skilled has exactly one alignment source of truth: the three-part interface\nbelow. Later coverage and activation work must consume this interface rather than\nre-derive a second RESOURCE_MAP parser or a local eligibility map.\n\n1. **Doc pointer.** This file plus the sk-code-skilled `SKILL.md` SMART ROUTING\n   block, which record that the `sk-code-router-sync.vitest.ts` suite was\n   retired, that `verify-router-sync.cjs` restores its checks, and what covers\n   each (section 3, \"Router-sync guard\"). The markdown-blind\n   `verify_alignment_drift.py` is not that authority.\n2. **Bijection module.** `qualifiedIdToLeaf` in\n   `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/lib/leaf-resource-contract.cjs`\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"sed -n '195,270p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/javascript/quality-standards/security-testing-and-exemptions.md; echo \\\"===ALIGN 130-160===\\\"; sed -n '130,160p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/shared/alignment-verification-automation.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793742819643,"end":1793742819965}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793742819972,"sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","part":{"partID":"prt_1a367521e0019rVH98x0kIDpX6","sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","messageID":"msg_1a3673a78001DbsnDgL6EJzemy","type":"tool","id":"call_01_63ziilbhgf4xwqjchife9f8y","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"===SHELL STYLE 160-180===\"; sed -n '162,180p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/shell/style-guide/overview-structure-and-naming.md; echo \"===JS DUP EVIDENCE===\"; grep -n 'folder-discovery.ts' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/javascript/quality-standards/overview-modules-and-docs.md; echo \"===SKILL/ROUTER headings===\"; for f in .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/SKILL.md .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/ROUTER.md; do echo \"--$f\"; grep -n '^#\\{1,3\\} ' \"$f\"; done"},"output":"===SHELL STYLE 160-180===\n    str=\"${str//\\\\/\\\\\\\\}\"\n    str=\"${str//\\\"/\\\\\\\"}\"\n    printf '%s' \"$str\"\n}\n```\n\n**Exception**: a file sourced into an interactive shell gives every helper that its public functions call a plain prefixed name instead, such as `skilled_loop_resolve`. Agent tool shells, Claude Code's among them, are rebuilt from a function snapshot that drops names starting with a single underscore, so a public function that calls `_helper` there fails with `command not found`.\n\n**Evidence**: `.skilled/bin/skilled-loop-shell.sh`\n\n**Evidence**: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/lib/shell-common.sh:37-45`\n\n### Variables\n\n**Use**: `lowercase_with_underscores` for local variables:\n\n```bash\nlocal file_path=\"$1\"\nlocal output_dir=\"${2:-./output}\"\n===JS DUP EVIDENCE===\n137:**Evidence**: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts`\n155:**Evidence**: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts`\n===SKILL/ROUTER headings===\n--.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/SKILL.md\n11:# opencode Surface — System-Code Evidence\n29:## 1. WHEN THE HUB BUNDLES THIS\n37:## 2. REFERENCE MAP\n110:## 2b. SMART ROUTING\n120:## 3. SURFACE STANDARDS (the non-negotiables)\n148:## 4. ASSETS AND OTHER SURFACE AREAS — ON-DEMAND\n164:## 5. QUALITY CHECKLIST MAP\n--.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/ROUTER.md\n14:# opencode Surface — System-Code Evidence Router\n21:## 1. OVERVIEW\n31:## 2. INTENT MODEL\n46:## 3. MACHINE ROUTER\n54:# sk-code-skilled owns its intent -> reference/asset routing. Paths are relative to\n55:# this skill root. The parent sk-code hub RESOURCE_MAP is the union of this map\n56:# (re-prefixed with sk-code-skilled/) plus the\n57:# parent-owned universal/shared tier. The router-sync guard\n58:# (assets/scripts/verify-router-sync.cjs, leg 2) checks that equality.\n59:# verify_alignment_drift.py --check-router checks dead routes only, so it is not\n60:# the equality authority. Leg 1b of the same guard fails on any reference or asset doc that\n61:# no router names, so a new doc under references/ or assets/ needs a RESOURCE_MAP entry here.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"===SHELL STYLE 160-180===\n    str=\"${str//\\\\/\\\\\\\\}\"\n    str=\"${str//\\\"/\\\\\\\"}\"\n    printf '%s' \"$str\"\n}\n```\n\n**Exception**: a file sourced into an interactive shell gives every helper that its public functions call a plain prefixed name instead, such as `skilled_loop_resolve`. Agent tool shells, Claude Code's among them, are rebuilt from a function snapshot that drops names starting with a single underscore, so a public function that calls `_helper` there fails with `command not found`.\n\n**Evidence**: `.skilled/bin/skilled-loop-shell.sh`\n\n**Evidence**: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/lib/shell-common.sh:37-45`\n\n### Variables\n\n**Use**: `lowercase_with_underscores` for local variables:\n\n```bash\nlocal file_path=\"$1\"\nlocal output_dir=\"${2:-./output}\"\n===JS DUP EVIDENCE===\n137:**Evidence**: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts`\n155:**Evidence**: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts`\n===SKILL/ROUTER headings===\n--.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/SKILL.md\n11:# opencode Surface — System-Code Evidence\n29:## 1. WHEN THE HUB BUNDLES THIS\n37:## 2. REFERENCE MAP\n110:## 2b. SMART ROUTING\n120:## 3. SURFACE STANDARDS (the non-negotiables)\n148:## 4. ASSETS AND OTHER SURFACE AREAS — ON-DEMAND\n164:## 5. QUALITY CHECKLIST MAP\n--.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/ROUTER.md\n14:# opencode Surface — System-Code Evidence Router\n21:## 1. OVERVIEW\n31:## 2. INTENT MODEL\n46:## 3. MACHINE ROUTER\n54:# sk-code-skilled owns its intent -> reference/asset routing. Paths are relative to\n55:# this skill root. The parent sk-code hub RESOURCE_MAP is the union of this map\n56:# (re-prefixed with sk-code-skilled/) plus the\n57:# parent-owned universal/shared tier. The router-sync guard\n58:# (assets/scripts/verify-router-sync.cjs, leg 2) checks that equality.\n59:# verify_alignment_drift.py --check-router checks dead routes only, so it is not\n60:# the equality authority. Leg 1b of the same guard fails on any reference or asset doc that\n61:# no router names, so a new doc under references/ or assets/ needs a RESOURCE_MAP entry here.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"echo \\\"===SHELL STYLE 160-180===\\\"; sed -n '162,180p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/shell/style-guide/overview-structure-and-naming.md; echo \\\"===JS DUP EVIDENCE===\\\"; grep -n 'folder-discovery.ts' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/javascript/quality-standards/overview-modules-and-docs.md; echo \\\"===SKILL/ROUTER headings===\\\"; for f in .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/SKILL.md .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/ROUTER.md; do echo \\\"--$f\\\"; grep -