{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793742836973,"sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","part":{"partID":"prt_1a3679430001xHOkAl0d1uXjhA","sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","messageID":"msg_1a3677ba4001HamDlut72ihzNN","type":"tool","id":"call_00_mfl389ypaurs3jy4qgz05zan","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rln 'Provides focused .* guidance for' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets | wc -l; echo \"---\"; sed -n '20,30p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/rust/style-guide/formatting-and-imports.md; echo \"===P0 CHECKLIST===\"; sed -n '15,30p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/checklists/rust-checklist/p0-safety-and-boundary-discipline.md"},"output":"       0\n---\n\n### Purpose\n\nProvides focused Rust guidance for formatting rules & import/module ordering in the OpenCode development environment.\n\n### When to Use\n\n- Implementing or reviewing Rust code covered by this topic\n- Preserving TypeScript interoperability and deterministic behavior\n- Applying the corresponding Rust standards at an implementation boundary\n\n===P0 CHECKLIST===\nHard-blocking Rust safety and boundary checks for JavaScript-facing interop code.\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nThis split checklist protects DTO, error, panic, unsafe-code, adapter, and golden-fixture boundaries in Rust interop implementations.\n\n### Usage\n\nApply this file after the Rust parity P0 checklist and resolve every item before proceeding to P1 checks.\n\n---\n\n## 2. P0 - SAFETY & BOUNDARY DISCIPLINE\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"       0\n---\n\n### Purpose\n\nProvides focused Rust guidance for formatting rules & import/module ordering in the OpenCode development environment.\n\n### When to Use\n\n- Implementing or reviewing Rust code covered by this topic\n- Preserving TypeScript interoperability and deterministic behavior\n- Applying the corresponding Rust standards at an implementation boundary\n\n===P0 CHECKLIST===\nHard-blocking Rust safety and boundary checks for JavaScript-facing interop code.\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nThis split checklist protects DTO, error, panic, unsafe-code, adapter, and golden-fixture boundaries in Rust interop implementations.\n\n### Usage\n\nApply this file after the Rust parity P0 checklist and resolve every item before proceeding to P1 checks.\n\n---\n\n## 2. P0 - SAFETY & BOUNDARY DISCIPLINE\n\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"grep -rln 'Provides focused .* guidance for' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets | wc -l; echo \\\"---\\\"; sed -n '20,30p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/rust/style-guide/formatting-and-imports.md; echo \\\"===P0 CHECKLIST===\\\"; sed -n '15,30p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/checklists/rust-checklist/p0-safety-and-boundary-discipline.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793742836784,"end":1793742836973}}}}
