st lines=fs.readFileSync(p,\\\"utf8\\\").trim().split(\\\"\\\\n\\\");lines.forEach((l,i)=>{try{JSON.parse(l)}catch(e){console.log(\\\"BAD\\\",p,i+1,e.message);process.exit(1)}});console.log(\\\"OK\\\",p,lines.length)}'; node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode research --run-directory specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek --event-json specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/.executor-state/iter-007-event.json | head -2; node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research --artifact-dir specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek 2>&1 | tail -6\"}"},"time":{"start":1793742945066,"end":1793742946299}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1793742947020,"sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","part":{"id":"prt_1a36942cc0013HDhIAERhjbrI5","sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","messageID":"msg_1a3693183001wn6rsREc5PEj87","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"4ca0672ffae5ded5e2328994ff19b42eb200f865","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":561,"output":375,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":226688,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793742948492,"sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","part":{"id":"prt_1a369488c001GOFRWfWLZpn7Gp","sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","messageID":"msg_1a36942d10016BbQ9FGHbliAxm","type":"step-start","snapshot":"4ca0672ffae5ded5e2328994ff19b42eb200f865"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793742973746,"sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","part":{"partID":"prt_1a369a902001zRP2AcD7DbVXv7","sessionID":"ses_e5ca055c6ffeOZO66b0AKuGGW6","messageID":"msg_1a36942d10016BbQ9FGHbliAxm","type":"tool","id":"call_00_kxu67lmae5j7e6giv31oysvi","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 8: Template, Guidance and Validator Changes\n\n## Focus\n\nConvert the confirmed defect classes and the traced validator gaps into concrete template, authoring-guidance and validator changes, with a mechanical-checkability verdict and a precision estimate for each.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Mapped each confirmed defect class to the exact validator function and rule-data block that should own it.\n2. Used the lineage's 121-file fence-aware scan as a prototype for the proposed detectors and counted its current hits.\n3. Ranked the proposals by precision, migration risk and whether a human must still judge the result.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **Adjacent bold-label lines — mechanically checkable, high precision.** Add `render_bold_label_join`: outside fenced code, flag when two consecutive non-blank lines both start with `**Label**` and neither is a list item. On the 121-file corpus the detector found zero hits at HEAD and nine blocks in the pre-fix control, so it is a true-positive-only rule with negligible false-positive risk; make it blocking. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py:2008] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md:130]\n\n2. **Text directly above `---` — mechanically checkable, high precision.** Add `render_setext_hazard`: flag a non-blank, non-heading, non-list, non-table line immediately above a thematic break, because Markdown renders it as a setext H2. The current corpus has zero hits, the pre-fix control has the divider pattern the template encourages, and the check is a one-line lookbehind; make it blocking. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py:676] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md:77]\n\n3. **`OVERVIEW AND <topic>` with no overview — mechanically checkable for emptiness, partially for quality.** Add `render_overview_empty`: for every H2 whose text contains OVERVIEW, require a prose paragraph of at least 40 characters or a `### Purpose` / `### When to Use` subsection with body text before the next section; flag a heading that continues after `OVERVIEW AND` as blocking. Whether the prose is a *good* overview remains human judgment, but the current `runner-contract.md` case and the pre-fix cascade case are both caught mechanically. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/references/runner-contract.md:20] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/shared/assets/template-rules.json:321]\n\n4. **Related Resources missing or misplaced — mechanically checkable, high precision once the template settles the rule.** Add `render_related_last`: require a related section for `reference` and `asset`, and flag any same-or-higher-level heading after it. This catches the three confirmed misplacements (`ROUTER.md` §8, `sk-code-review/SKILL.md` §8, `alignment-verification-automation.md` §5) and the two confirmed omissions (`runner-contract.md`, `quality-config.md`). The template must first be made consistent: the asset template says \"must be last\", the reference template does not say it, and `template-rules.json` lists it as recommended only. Make all three say required-and-last, then enforce it. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md:166] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/shared/assets/template-rules.json:323] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/ROUTER.md:218]\n\n5. **Bare URLs — mechanically checkable, medium-high precision.** Add `render_bare_url`: outside fences and inline code, flag an `http(s)://` token that is not inside `[text](url)` and not an angle-bracket autolink. The current corpus has zero hits; the pre-fix control has nine. Keep it a warning for one migration window because command examples and generated text can carry intentional raw URLs. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md:58] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md:28 (at cd00629166)]\n\n6. **Duplicated content — exact duplicates checkable, semantic duplication not.** Add `render_duplicate_block` for an identical paragraph or an identical bold-label line repeated inside one section (warning), which catches the current `web-performance-and-loading.md:130` doubled support sentence and the `shell/style-guide/overview-structure-and-naming.md:170/172` repeated Evidence label. The 14-file rust boilerplate is *not* catchable this way: it is semantic sameness with different topic words, so it needs a batch-level \"repeated purpose sentence\" heuristic (medium precision) plus editorial review. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md:130] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/shell/style-guide/overview-structure-and-naming.md:170] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/rust/style-guide/naming-conventions.md:22]\n\n7. **Numbering and item order — mechanically checkable proxies, medium precision.** Extend the H2 regex to `^## (\\d+)([a-z]?)\\.` and make a letter suffix or a non-sequential number blocking, which catches `## 2b.` in two skill bodies and the unnumbered run in `pr-state-dedup.md`. Add a rule-id monotonic check for `^### ([A-Z]{1,4})(\\d+)\\.` as a warning, which catches P10 before P8 and the missing I8. Neither proves the order matches the reader's task; a monotonic id sequence is only a proxy for authoring-history ordering. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py:736] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md:111] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/pr-state-dedup.md:21]\n\n8. **Template and guidance changes — the precondition for every mechanical check.** Rewrite the reference template's Section 1/§3 duplication into one \"when to create\" section; add three rules the templates currently omit: (a) a bold-label line is a list item or is followed by a blank line and body text, (b) a thematic break always has a blank line above it, (c) an overview may not be titled `OVERVIEW AND <topic>`. Add the related-last clause to the *reference* template, and make the skill template's numbered-H2 rule reject letter suffixes. Without these, a validator rule would contradict the document authors are told to copy. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md:36] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md:182] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-md-template.md:65]\n\n9. **What stays human.** \"Items ordered by authoring history instead of reader task\" at the semantic level, \"misplaced content\" beyond heading position, and whether an overview actually orients a reader cannot be decided by a regex. The validator can surface the proxies above; the review checklist must ask a human to read the rendered page and confirm the narrative order. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py:2009]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A validator rule that rejects every bold-label paragraph: separate label paragraphs are legitimate; only adjacency is a rendering defect.\n- A validator rule that rejects every raw URL: fenced command examples and generated reports can carry them; only unfenced, unlinked prose URLs are the defect.\n- A cross-file \"same purpose sentence\" rule as blocking: the rust boilerplate differs by topic word and would need fuzzy matching, which is too imprecise for a blocking gate.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Trying to make \"reader-task order\" fully mechanical: no static analysis can know the reader's task; monotonic ids and related-last are the only defensible proxies.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"mechanically checkable\" is reported as three levels — exact (adjacency, setext, empty overview, related-last), proxy (numbering, rule-id order, duplicate blocks) and judgment (semantic order, overview quality).\n- Contradictory evidence: the asset template and the rule data disagree on whether related resources are optional; the proposal requires resolving that conflict before enforcement, not after.\n- Missing dependencies: none.\n- Partial success: precision estimates come from a 121-file prototype scan and one known-bad control, not from a labelled corpus; they are directional, not measured error rates.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py:676-938`, `:1937-2058`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/shared/assets/template-rules.json:319-345`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md:36-213`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md:129-174`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-md-template.md:65`\n- lineage scan prototype: `.executor-state/scan.cjs` over 121 scoped files\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.85\n- Questions addressed: per-class remediation, mechanical checkability, precision.\n- Questions answered: \"Which template, guidance and validator changes would catch each defect class, and which are mechanically checkable at what precision?\"\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: using the prototype scan's hit counts turned \"mechanically checkable\" into a ranked list with real false-positive evidence rather than an assertion.\n- What did not work and why: precision cannot be claimed as a measured error rate from one control file; the findings label the estimates as directional.\n- What I would do differently: label a small corpus of intentional label paragraphs and intentional raw URLs before claiming a precision number for those two rules.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nSynthesis: consolidate the eight iterations into `research.md`, state the residual unknowns (no labelled precision corpus, no full read of every skilled rule body), and record the stop reason as `maxIterationsReached`.\n","path":"specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-008.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-008.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-008.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 8: Template, Guidance and Validator Changes\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nConvert the confirmed defect classes and the traced validator gaps into concrete template, authoring-guidance and validator changes, with a mechanical-checkability verdict and a precision estimate for each.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Mapped each confirmed defect class to the exact validator function and rule-data block that should own it.\\n2. Used the lineage's 121-file fence-aware scan as a prototype for the proposed detectors and counted its current hits.\\n3. Ranked the proposals by precision, migration risk and whether a human must still judge the result.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. **Adjacent bold-label lines — mechanically checkable, high precision.** Add `render_bold_label_join`: outside fenced code, flag when two consecutive non-blank lines both start with `**Label**` and neither is a list item. On the 121-file corpus the detector found zero hits at HEAD and nine blocks in the pre-fix control, so it is a true-positive-only rule with negligible false-positive risk; make it blocking. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py:2008] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md:130]\\n\\n2. **Text directly above `---` — mechanically checkable, high precision.** Add `render_setext_hazard`: flag a non-blank, non-heading, non-list, non-table line immediately above a thematic break, because Markdown renders it as a setext H2. The current corpus has zero hits, the pre-fix control has the divider pattern the template encourages, and the check is a one-line lookbehind; make it blocking. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py:676] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md:77]\\n\\n3. **`OVERVIEW AND <topic>` with no overview — mechanically checkable for emptiness, partially for quality.** Add `render_overview_empty`: for every H2 whose text contains OVERVIEW, require a prose paragraph of at least 40 characters or a `### Purpose` / `### When to Use` subsection with body text before the next section; flag a heading that continues after `OVERVIEW AND` as blocking. Whether the prose is a *good* overview remains human judgment, but the current `runner-contract.md` case and the pre-fix cascade case are both caught mechanically. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/references/runner-contract.md:20] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/shared/assets/template-rules.json:321]\\n\\n4. **Related Resources missing or misplaced — mechanically checkable, high precision once the template settles the rule.** Add `render_related_last`: require a related section for `reference` and `asset`, and flag any same-or-higher-level heading after it. This catches the three confirmed misplacements (`ROUTER.md` §8, `sk-code-review/SKILL.md` §8, `alignment-verification-automation.md` §5) and the two confirmed omissions (`runner-contract.md`, `quality-config.md`). The template must first be made consistent: the asset template says \\\"must be last\\\", the reference template does not say it, and `template-rules.json` lists it as recommended only. Make all three say required-and-last, then enforce it. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md:166] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/shared/assets/template-rules.json:323] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/ROUTER.md:218]\\n\\n5. **Bare URLs — mechanically checkable, medium-high precision.** Add `render_bare_url`: outside fences and inline code, flag an `http(s)://` token that is not inside `[text](url)` and not an angle-bracket autolink. The current corpus has zero hits; the pre-fix control has nine. Keep it a warning for one migration window because command examples and generated text can carry intentional raw URLs. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md:58] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md:28 (at cd00629166)]\\n\\n6. **Duplicated content — exact duplicates checkable, semantic duplication not.** Add `render_duplicate_block` for an identical paragraph or an identical bold-label line repeated inside one section (warning), which catches the current `web-performance-and-loading.md:130` doubled support sentence and the `shell/style-guide/overview-structure-and-naming.md:170/172` repeated Evidence label. The 14-file rust boilerplate is *not* catchable this way: it is semantic sameness with different topic words, so it needs a batch-level \\\"repeated purpose sentence\\\" heuristic (medium precision) plus editorial review. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md:130] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/shell/style-guide/overview-structure-and-naming.md:170] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/rust/style-guide/naming-conventions.md:22]\\n\\n7. **Numbering and item order — mechanically checkable proxies, medium precision.** Extend the H2 regex to `^## (\\\\d+)([a-z]?)\\\\.` and make a letter suffix or a non-sequential number blocking, which catches `## 2b.` in two skill bodies and the unnumbered run in `pr-state-dedup.md`. Add a rule-id monotonic check for `^### ([A-Z]{1,4})(\\\\d+)\\\\.` as a warning, which catches P10 before P8 and the missing I8. Neither proves the order matches the reader's task; a monotonic id sequence is only a proxy for authoring-history ordering. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py:736] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-performance-and-loading.md:111] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/pr-state-dedup.md:21]\\n\\n8. **Template and guidance changes — the precondition for every mechanical check.** Rewrite the reference template's Section 1/§3 duplication into one \\\"when to create\\\" section; add three rules the templates currently omit: (a) a bold-label line is a list item or is followed by a blank line and body text, (b) a thematic break always has a blank line above it, (c) an overview may not be titled `OVERVIEW AND <topic>`. Add the related-last clause to the *reference* template, and make the skill template's numbered-H2 rule reject letter suffixes. Without these, a validator rule would contradict the document authors are told to copy. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md:36] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md:182] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-md-template.md:65]\\n\\n9. **What stays human.** \\\"Items ordered by authoring history instead of reader task\\\" at the semantic level, \\\"misplaced content\\\" beyond heading position, and whether an overview actually orients a reader cannot be decided by a regex. The validator can surface the proxies above; the review checklist must ask a human to read the rendered page and confirm the narrative order. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py:2009]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A validator rule that rejects every bold-label paragraph: separate label paragraphs are legitimate; only adjacency is a rendering defect.\\n- A validator rule that rejects every raw URL: fenced command examples and generated reports can carry them; only unfenced, unlinked prose URLs are the defect.\\n- A cross-file \\\"same purpose sentence\\\" rule as blocking: the rust boilerplate differs by topic word and would need fuzzy matching, which is too imprecise for a blocking gate.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Trying to make \\\"reader-task order\\\" fully mechanical: no static analysis can know the reader's task; monotonic ids and related-last are the only defensible proxies.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"mechanically checkable\\\" is reported as three levels — exact (adjacency, setext, empty overview, related-last), proxy (numbering, rule-id order, duplicate blocks) and judgment (semantic order, overview quality).\\n- Contradictory evidence: the asset template and the rule data disagree on whether related resources are optional; the proposal requires resolving that conflict before enforcement, not after.\\n- Missing dependencies: none.\\n- Partial success: precision estimates come from a 121-file prototype scan and one known-bad control, not from a labelled corpus; they are directional, not measured error rates.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py:676-938`, `:1937-2058`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/shared/assets/template-rules.json:319-345`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-reference-template.md:36-213`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-asset-template.md:129-174`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-md-template.md:65`\\n- lineage scan prototype: `.executor-state/scan.cjs` over 121 scoped files\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.85\\n- Questions addressed: per-class remediation, mechanical checkability, precision.\\n- Questions answered: \\\"Which template, guidance and validator changes would catch each defect class, and which are mechanically checkable at what precision?\\\"\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: using the prototype scan's hit counts turned \\\"mechanically checkable\\\" into a ranked list with real false-positive evidence rather than an assertion.\\n- What did not work and why: precision cannot be claimed as a measured error rate from one control file; the findings label the estimates as directional.\\n- What I would do differently: label a small corpus of intentional label paragraphs and intentional raw URLs before claiming a precision number for those two rules.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nSynthesis: consolidate the eight iterations into `research.md`, state the residual unknowns (no labelled precision corpus, no full read of every skilled rule body), and record the stop reason as `maxIterationsReached`.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/sk-code/018-frontend-upstream-proposals/010-reference-readability-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-008.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793742973186,"end":1793742973746}}}}
